k. Let's add 1,462 + 657,900 first, then add 43,860. 1,462 + 657,900 = 659,362. Then +43,860: 659,362 +40,000 = 699,362 +3,860 = 703,222. Same result. Okay.\n\nHmm, so I think that's correct. Let me see if there's another way to check. Maybe divide the result by one of the numbers to see if I get the other.\n\nLet's try dividing 703,222 \u00f7 731 and see if it equals 962.\n\nFirst, approximate: 731 \u00d7 900 = 657,900. Subtract that from 703,222: 703,222 - 657,900 = 45,322. Now, 731 \u00d7 60 = 43,860. So 45,322 -43,860 = 1,462. Then 731 \u00d72 =1,462. So total is 900+60+2=962. That's exactly the division. So that checks out.\n\nAlternatively, divide 703,222 by 962 to see if it's 731. Let me try that.\n\n962 \u00d7 700 = 673,400. Subtract that from 703,222: 703,222 -673,400 =29,822.\n\nNow, 962 \u00d730 =28,860. Subtract: 29,822 -28,860 = 962.\n\nThen 962 \u00d71 =962. So total is 700+30+1=731. Perfect. So that confirms the answer is correct.\n\nTherefore, after double-checking, I'm confident the product is 703,222.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 731 and 962 is \\boxed{703222}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 731 and 962, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 962.\n\n1. **Multiply 731 by the ones place digit (2) of 962:**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 2 = 1462\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 731 by the tens place digit (60) of 962:**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 60 = 731 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 4386 \\times 10 = 43860\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 731 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 962:**\n   \\[\n   731 \\times 900 = 731 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 6579 \\times 100 = 657900\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   1462 + 43860 + 657900\n   \\]\n\n   - First, add \\(1462\\) and \\(43860\\):\n     \\[\n     1462 + 43860 = 45322\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(657900\\):\n     \\[\n     45322 + 657900 = 703222\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 731 and 962 is \\(\\boxed{703222}\\).",
