own further:\n\nAlternatively, 212 \u00d7916 = (200 +12) \u00d7 (900 +16).\n\nBut that might be more complex. Alternatively, compute 212 \u00d7 916 as:\n\nFirst, 212 \u00d7 900 = 190,800.\n\nThen 212 \u00d716 = ?\n\n212 \u00d710 =2120; 212 \u00d76=1272. So 2120+1272 = 3392.\n\nAdding them together: 190,800 + 3,392 = 194,192. Same result. Okay, so that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, use a calculator? Well, since I can't, but let me do another verification.\n\nLet me compute 212 \u00d7 916:\n\nLet me compute 200\u00d7916 = 183,200.\n\nThen 12\u00d7916 = ?\n\n10\u00d7916 =9,160.\n\n2\u00d7916=1,832.\n\nSo 9,160 +1,832 =10,992.\n\nAdding to 183,200: 183,200 +10,992 =194,192. Yep, same answer.\n\nSo that seems correct. Therefore, the product is 194,192. So the steps are as follows:\n\nMultiply 212 by 6 (ones place): 1272.\n\nMultiply 212 by 10 (tens place):2120.\n\nMultiply 212 by 900 (hundreds place):190,800.\n\nAdd them all: 1272 +2120 =3392; 3392 +190,800 =194,192.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 194,192.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 212 and 916 is \\boxed{194192}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 212 and 916, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 212 by the ones place digit (6) of 916:**\n   \\[\n   212 \\times 6 = 1272\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 212 by the tens place digit (10) of 916:**\n   \\[\n   212 \\times 10 = 2120\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 212 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 916:**\n   \\[\n   212 \\times 900 = 190800\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n1272 + 2120 + 190800\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the first two steps:\n\\[\n1272 + 2120 = 3392\n\\]\n\nThen add this result to the third step's result:\n\\[\n3392 + 190800 = 194192\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{194192}\\).",
