\n\nTens:8+0=8\n\nHundreds:4 +6 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\nThousands:5 +9 =14 +1 (carryover) =15 \u2192 write 5, carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands:1 +6 =7 +1 (carryover) =8\n\nSo the total is 85,086.\n\nWait, that seems right. Let me confirm with another method. Alternatively, 15,486 +69,600 = 15,486 +69,600. Let's compute 15,486 +70,000 =85,486, then subtract 400 (since 69,600 is 70,000 -400). So 85,486 -400 =85,086. Yep, that checks out.\n\nTherefore, the total sum of the partial products is 85,086. So the final product of 174 and 489 is 85,086. Let me just verify once more using another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, multiply 174 \u00d7489 directly:\n\nAlternatively, using the standard algorithm:\n\n\u202f\u202f\u202f174\n\n\u00d7489\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 174 by 9: 1,566\n\nThen multiply 174 by 80 (shift one position): 13,920\n\nThen multiply 174 by 400 (shift two positions):69,600\n\nAdding those gives the same as before: 1,566 +13,920=15,486; 15,486 +69,600=85,086. So that's consistent.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use another approach like distributive property:\n\n174\u00d7489 =174\u00d7(500 -11) =174\u00d7500 -174\u00d711.\n\n174\u00d7500 =87,000\n\n174\u00d711 =1,914\n\nThus, 87,000 -1,914 =85,086. That matches. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator verification? Since I can't use a calculator, but the multiple methods all lead to the same result, so confident it's 85,086.\n\nAlright, so putting this into the template:\n\nThe question is the product of 174 and 489. The reasoning should follow the steps of multiplying by each digit's place and summing. Let me structure it according to the example given.\n\nOriginal example's reasoning:\n\n1. Multiply number1 by the ones place digit of number2.\n\n2. Multiply number1 by the tens place digit (as a multiple of 10) of number2.\n\n3. Multiply number1 by the hundreds place digit (as a multiple of 100) of number2.\n\nThen sum all those.\n\nSo in this case:\n\n1. Multiply 174 by 9 (the ones place of 489) \u2192 1,566\n\n2. Multiply 174 by 80 (the tens place, which is 8\u00d710) \u219213,920\n\n3. Multiply 174 by 400 (the hundreds place, which is 4\u00d7100) \u219269,600\n\nSum them: 1,566 +13,920 +69,600 =85,086.\n\nTherefore, the answer is 85,086. I need to present this in the template as per the user's instruction. Let me check the template again.\n\nThe user provided the example with 27 and 153. The reasoning was broken down into steps corresponding to each digit's place. The answer section then sums them.\n\nSo applying to the current problem:\n\n# Reasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 489 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 174 by the ones place digit 9 of 489: 174 \u00d7 9 = 1,566.\n\n2. Multiply 174 by the tens place digit 80 of 489: 174 \u00d7 80 = 13,920.\n\n3. Multiply 174 by the hundreds place digit 400 of 489: 174 \u00d7 400 = 69,600.\n\nAnswer:\n\nNow, sum all the step results: 1,566 + 13,920 + 69,600 = 85,086.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 85,086.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me just ensure that all the multiplication steps are correctly written and the sum is accurate. The numbers add up as before. Alright, looks good. So that's the solution.\n</think>\n\n",
