e try that:\n\n523 \u00d7 193:\n\nFirst, 523 \u00d7 3 = 1,569\n\nThen 523 \u00d7 90 = 523 \u00d7 9 \u00d7 10. 523\u00d79: 4,707. So 47,070.\n\nThen 523 \u00d7 100 = 52,300.\n\nAdding those three: 1,569 + 47,070 = 48,639; then +52,300 = 100,939. Yep, same result.\n\nOkay, so all methods lead to 100,939. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 193 and 523?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 523 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three parts.  \n1. Multiply 193 by the ones place digit (3):  \n   \\(193 \\times 3 = 579\\)  \n2. Multiply 193 by the tens place digit (20):  \n   \\(193 \\times 20 = 3,\\!860\\)  \n3. Multiply 193 by the hundreds place digit (500):  \n   \\(193 \\times 500 = 96,\\!500\\)  \n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(579 + 3,\\!860 + 96,\\!500 = 100,\\!939\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nThe final computed product is \\boxed{100939}.",
