 505 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   505 \\times 6 = 3030\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 505 by the tens place digit (50):**\n   \\[\n   505 \\times 50 = 25250\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 505 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   505 \\times 900 = 454500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three multiplications:\n\\[\n3030 + 25250 + 454500\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(3030\\) and \\(25250\\):\n\\[\n3030 + 25250 = 28280\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to \\(454500\\):\n\\[\n28280 + 454500 = 482780\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{482780}\\).",
