, for 820, it's 0 (ones), 20 (tens), and 800 (hundreds). So the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 415 by 0 (the ones digit)\n2. Multiply 415 by 20 (the tens place)\n3. Multiply 415 by 800 (the hundreds place)\n\nThen sum all three. \n\nSo following that structure:\n\nStep 1: 415 × 0 = 0\n\nStep 2: 415 × 20 = 8,300\n\nStep 3: 415 × 800 = 332,000\n\nAdding them: 0 + 8,300 + 332,000 = 340,300. So that's exactly the same as before. \n\nI think that's correct. So the final answer should be 340,300. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations. Maybe check one of the multiplications again:\n\n415 × 20: 415 × 2 = 830, so ×20 is 8,300. Correct.\n\n415 × 800: 415 ×8 = 3,320, so ×800 is 3,320 ×100 = 332,000. Correct.\n\nYes, so all steps check out. The sum is indeed 340,300. Alright, I think that's solid.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 415 and 820?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 820 has three digits, so we can break it down into three steps:\n1. Multiply 415 by the ones place digit (0):  \n   \\(415 \\times 0 = 0\\).  \n2. Multiply 415 by the tens place digit (20):  \n   \\(415 \\times 20 = 8,\\!300\\).  \n3. Multiply 415 by the hundreds place digit (800):  \n   \\(415 \\times 800 = 332,\\!000\\).  \n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(0 + 8,\\!300 + 332,\\!000 = 340,\\!300\\).  \n\nSo, the final computed product is **340,300**.", '']
