n): \n\n790 x 9 = 7,110, so with the zero it's 71,100.\n\nThen multiply 790 by 100 (the 1 in the hundreds place, shifted two positions): 79,000.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n6,320\n\n+71,100\n\n= 77,420\n\n+79,000\n\n= 156,420. \n\nYep, same result. So I'm confident that's correct. I think the answer is 156,420.\n\nWait, but let me check with a calculator just to be 100% sure. Since I don't have a calculator here, but maybe do another manual check.\n\nAlternatively, let's compute 790 * 200 = 158,000. Then subtract 790*2=1,580. So 158,000 - 1,580: \n\n158,000 - 1,000 is 157,000, then subtract 580 more: 157,000 - 500 = 156,500, then minus 80 is 156,420. Yep, that's the same. \n\nAlright, so all methods confirm that 790 multiplied by 198 is 156,420. I think that's solid. The reasoning steps as per the template would follow the three-digit breakdown of 198 into hundreds, tens, and ones, multiplying each by 790 and then summing. So the answer should be 156,420.\n</think>", '']
