4 is in thousands place of the second? Wait, actually, 34,090 has 4 in thousands place, and 3,896 has 3 in thousands place. So 3 (thousands) +4 (thousands) =7 thousands. Then the ten thousands place is 3 from the 34,090. So total is 37,986. Okay, so that's 37,986.\n\nThen add the third part, which is 48,700.\n\nSo 37,986 +48,700.\n\nLet me compute that:.\n\n37,986 +48,700.\n\nAdding the thousands:.\n\n37,000 +48,000 =85,000.\n\nThen 986 +700 =1,686</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
