 \\boxed{325822}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 629 and 518?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 518 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 629 by the ones place digit (8) of 518:\n   \\[\n   629 \\times 8 = 5032\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 629 by the tens place digit (10) of 518:\n   \\[\n   629 \\times 10 = 6290\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 629 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 518:\n   \\[\n   629 \\times 500 = 314500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n5032 + 6290 + 314500 = 325822\n\\]\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(5032 + 6290 + 314500 = 325822\\).\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{325822}.", '']
