lt, I feel confident it's correct.\n\nSo the product of 846 and 105 is 88,830.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 846 and 105 is \\boxed{88830}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 846 and 105?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 105 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 846 by the ones place digit (5) of 105:  \n   \\( 846 \\times 5 = 4230 \\).\n2. Multiply 846 by the tens place digit (0) of 105:  \n   \\( 846 \\times 0 = 0 \\).  \n   (This result is shifted one position to the left, but remains 0.)\n3. Multiply 846 by the hundreds place digit (1) of 105:  \n   \\( 846 \\times 1 = 846 \\).  \n   (This result is shifted two positions to the left, becoming \\( 84600 \\).)\n\nSum all the step results:  \n\\( 4230 + 0 + 84600 = 88830 \\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 4230 + 0 + 84600 = 88830 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{88830}.",
