nal 410, so 12,054 x10 = 120,540. Yep, same answer again. Okay, so that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 120,540. I can't see any mistakes in my calculations, and multiple methods confirm it. So I feel confident about this answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 294 and 410 is \\boxed{120540}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 294 and 410, we can break down the multiplication using place values and the distributive property.\n\n1. **Multiply 294 by the ones place digit (0) of 410:**\n   \\[\n   294 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 294 by the tens place digit (10) of 410:**\n   \\[\n   294 \\times 10 = 2940\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 294 by the hundreds place digit (400) of 410:**\n   \\[\n   294 \\times 400 = 294 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 1176 \\times 100 = 117600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results from the steps above:**\n   \\[\n   0 + 2940 + 117600 = 120540\n   \\]\n\nThus, the product of 294 and 410 is \\(\\boxed{120540}\\).",
