d 157 is \\boxed{84152}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 536 and 157, we break down the multiplication step by step using the standard algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 536 by the ones place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   536 \\times 7 = 3752\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(6 \\times 7 = 42\\), carry over 4; \\(3 \\times 7 + 4 = 25\\), carry over 2; \\(5 \\times 7 + 2 = 37\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 536 by the tens place digit (50):**\n   \\[\n   536 \\times 50 = 26800\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(536 \\times 5 = 2680\\), then multiply by 10 to shift one position: \\(2680 \\times 10 = 26800\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 536 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   536 \\times 100 = 53600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   3752 + 26800 + 53600\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(3752 + 26800 = 30552\\)\n   - Then add \\(30552 + 53600 = 84152\\)\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{84152}\\).", '']
