      "text": "350,900. Wait, hold on. Let me check the addition again. 48,400 plus 302,500. 48,400 + 300,000 is 348,400. Then add the remaining 2,500: 348,400 +2,500 = 350,900. That seems correct.\n\nWait a second, but let me cross-verify using another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 605 by 580:\n\nFirst, write 605 \u00d7 580.\n\nAlternatively, since 580 is 58 \u00d710, so 605 \u00d758 \u00d710. Let me compute 605 \u00d758 first.\n\n605 \u00d758:\n\nBreakdown: 605 \u00d750 and 605 \u00d78.\n\n605 \u00d750: 605 \u00d75 = 3025, then \u00d710 is 30,250.\n\n605 \u00d78 = 4,840 (as before).\n\nAdding those together: 30,250 +4,840 = 35,090.\n\nThen multiply by 10 (since we did \u00d758 instead of \u00d7580): 35,090 \u00d710 = 350,900. Okay, same result. That matches. So that's good.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do it the long multiplication way:\n\n       605\n     \u00d7580\n     -------\nFirst multiply by the 0 (ones place): 605\u00d70=0, write down 0.\n\nThen multiply by 8 (tens place, so shifted one position left): 605\u00d78=4840, so written as 48400.\n\nThen multiply by 5 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left): 605\u00d75=3025, but shifted two places becomes 302500.\n\nNow add them:\n\n    0\n+48400\n+302500\n= 350,900. Yep, same result.\n\nSo I think that's correct. Therefore, the product of 605 and 580 is 350,900.\n\nWait, but let me check with another method just to be thorough. Maybe using distributive property:\n\n605 \u00d7580 = 605 \u00d7 (500 + 80 +0) = 605\u00d7500 +605\u00d780 +605\u00d70. Which is exactly what I did earlier, so that's consistent. So all methods lead to 350,900. I think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes here. So I can confidently say the answer is 350,900.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 605 and 580 is \\boxed{350900}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 605 and 580, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 580:\n\n1. **Multiply 605 by the ones place digit (0):**\n   \\[\n   605 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 605 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   605 \\times 80 = 605 \\times (8 \\times 10) = (605 \\times 8) \\times 10\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(605 \\times 8\\):\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 8 = 4800 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 5 \\times 8 = 40\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   4800 + 40 = 4840\n   \\]\n   Then multiply by 10:\n   \\[\n   4840 \\times 10 = 48400\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 605 by the hundreds place digit (500):**\n   \\[\n   605 \\times 500 = 605 \\times (5 \\times 100) = (605 \\times 5) \\times 100\n   \\]\n   Calculate \\(605 \\times 5\\):\n   \\[\n   600 \\times 5 = 3000 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 5 \\times 5 = 25\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3000 + 25 = 3025\n   \\]\n   Then multiply by 100:\n   \\[\n   3025 \\times 100 = 302500\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the results:**\n\\[\n0 + 48400 + 302500 = 350900\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 605 and 580 is \\(\\boxed{350900}\\).",
