erence would be (150-1)*(170+3) =150\u00d7173 -1\u00d7173. Wait, maybe that's complicating. Alternatively, 149\u00d7173 = (150-1)*(170+3) =150\u00d7170 +150\u00d73 -1\u00d7170 -1\u00d73 =25,500 +450 -170 -3 =25,500+450 is 25,950; 25,950 -170 is 25,780; then minus 3 is 25,777. Yes, that matches exactly. So that confirms it's correct.\n\nSo the answer is 25,777.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 149 and 173 is \\boxed{25777}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 149 and 173?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 173 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 149 by the ones place digit 3 of 173:  \n   \\( 149 \\times 3 = 447 \\)\n2. Multiply 149 by the tens place digit 70 of 173:  \n   \\( 149 \\times 70 = 10430 \\)\n3. Multiply 149 by the hundreds place digit 100 of 173:  \n   \\( 149 \\times 100 = 14900 \\)\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 447 + 10430 + 14900 = 25777 \\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is 25777.\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 149 and 173 is \\boxed{25777}.",
