e hundreds digit (2), which is 257×2 (but since it's hundreds place, 2×100, so 257×2×100=51,400.\n\nThen sum all three: 771 +0 +51,400=52,171. That's exactly the steps. So I think the reasoning is correct. I don't see any mistakes here. So the final answer is 52,171.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 257 and 203 is \\boxed{52171}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 257 and 203?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 203 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 257 by the ones place digit (3) of 203:\n   \\[\n   257 \\times 3 = 771\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 257 by the tens place digit (0) of 203. Since the tens digit is 0, this results in 0:\n   \\[\n   257 \\times 0 = 0 \\quad (\\text{shifted one position to the left, resulting in } 0)\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 257 by the hundreds place digit (2) of 203 (which is equivalent to multiplying by 200):\n   \\[\n   257 \\times 200 = 51400\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n771 + 0 + 51400 = 52171\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{52171}.", '']
