hink that's correct.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 361 and 476?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 476 has three digits, so we can break it into three parts:  \n1. Multiply 361 by the **ones place digit (6)** of 476:  \n   \\( 361 \\times 6 = 2,\\!166 \\).  \n2. Multiply 361 by the **tens place digit (70)** of 476:  \n   \\( 361 \\times 70 = 25,\\!270 \\).  \n3. Multiply 361 by the **hundreds place digit (400)** of 476:  \n   \\( 361 \\times 400 = 144,\\!400 \\).  \n\n**Sum all the step results:**  \n\\( 2,\\!166 + 25,\\!270 + 144,\\!400 = 171,\\!836 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 2,\\!166 + 25,\\!270 + 144,\\!400 = 171,\\!836 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{171836}.", '']
