    317  \n    ×996  \n    -------\n      1902  (317×6)\n     28530  (317×90, shifted one position)\n    285300  (317×900, shifted two positions)\n    -------\n    315732\n\nAdding those: 1902 + 28530 = 30432. Then 30432 + 285300 = 315,732. Yep, same result. So I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 317 and 996 is \\boxed{315732}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 317 and 996, we can break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 996 (hundreds, tens, and ones):\n\n1. **Multiply 317 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 6 = 1902\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 317 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 90 = 317 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 2853 \\times 10 = 28530\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 317 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   317 \\times 900 = 317 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 2853 \\times 100 = 285300\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n1902 + 28530 + 285300\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n1902 + 28530 = 30432\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result of the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n30432 + 285300 = 315732\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 317 and 996 is \\(\\boxed{315732}\\).", '']
