n\n4*2 =8\n\nAdding all together: 195,000 +600 is 195,600; plus 2,600 is 198,200; plus 8 is 198,208. Yep, that matches. So that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 198,208. I think that's solid. I don't see any errors in the steps. The initial breakdown into partial products and their addition all add up correctly. The cross-verification using different methods gives the same result. So I'm confident the answer is correct.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 304 and 652?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 652 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps based on place value.\n1. Multiply 304 by the ones place digit (2):  \n   \\(304 \\times 2 = 608\\).  \n2. Multiply 304 by the tens place digit (50):  \n   \\(304 \\times 50 = 15,200\\).  \n3. Multiply 304 by the hundreds place digit (600):  \n   \\(304 \\times 600 = 182,400\\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(608 + 15,200 + 182,400 = 198,208\\).  \n\nSo, the final computed product is **198,208**.", '']
