oxed{429825}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 825 and 521?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 521 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps.\n1. Multiply 825 by the ones place digit 1 of 521:  \n   \\( 825 \\times 1 = 825 \\).\n\n2. Multiply 825 by the tens place digit 20 of 521:  \n   \\( 825 \\times 20 = 16,\\!500 \\).\n\n3. Multiply 825 by the hundreds place digit 500 of 521:  \n   \\( 825 \\times 500 = 412,\\!500 \\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\( 825 + 16,\\!500 + 412,\\!500 = 429,\\!825 \\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{429825}\\).",
