600. Alternatively, 819*4 = 3,276, so times 100 would be 327,600. Either way, same result. Good.\n\nNow I need to add up all three parts: 7,371 (from the ones place), plus 16,380 (from the tens), plus 327,600 (from the hundreds). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 7,371 + 16,380. Let's see, 7,000 + 16,000 is 23,000. Then 371 + 380 is 751. So total is 23,751. Then add that to 327,600. .\n\n23,751 + 327,600. Let's break it down again. 23,000 + 327,000 = 350,000. Then 751 + 600 = 1,351. Wait, no, that's not right. Wait, 23,751 + 327,600. Maybe better to add them directly:.\n\n327,600.\n+ 23,751.\n= ?.\n\nStarting from the right: 0 +1 is 1, 0+5 is 5, 6+7 is 13, so carry over 1. Then 7 + 3 + 1 (carry) is 11, so that's 1 in the thousands place and carry over 1. Then 2 + 3 (from 327) plus the carried 1 is 6. Wait, maybe I should write it out:.\n\n327,600.\n+\xa0 23,751.\n----------.\nAdding units place: 0 +1 =1.\nTens: 0 +5=5.\nHundreds:6 +7=13, write down 3, carry 1.\nThousands:7 +3 +1 (carry) =11, write 1, carry 1.\nTen-thousands: 2 +2 (from 23,751's 2 in the ten-thousands place? Wait, 23,751 is only 5 digits: 2 (ten thousands?), no, 23,751 is 2 (ten thousands?), wait, 23,751 is 2 (ten thousands?), 3 (thousands?), 7 (hundreds?), 5 (tens?), 1 (ones). Wait, 23,751 is 2*10,000 + 3*1,000 + 7*100 +5*10 +1. So adding to 327,600:.\n\n327,600 is 3 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands), 6 (hundreds), 0 (tens), 0 (ones).\n\nSo:.\n\n327,600.\n+ 23,751.\n= ?.\n\nStart from right:.\nOnes: 0 +1 =1.\nTens:0+5=5.\nHundreds:6 +7=13. Write 3, carryover 1.\nThousands place:7 (from 327,600) +3 (from 23,751's thousands) +1 (carryover) =11. So write 1, carryover 1.\nTen-thousands place:2 (from 327,600's ten-thousands) +2 (from 23,751's ten-thousands?) Wait, 23,751 has 2 in the ten-thousands place? Wait no, 23,751 is 2*10,000, so yes. So 2 (from 327,600's ten-thousands?) Wait, 327,600 is 3 (hundred thousands), 2 (ten thousands), 7 (thousands). So the ten-thousands digit 