  \\[\n   818 \\times 10 = 8180\n   \\]\n   - Since the tens place digit is 1, we multiply by 10, resulting in 8180.\n\n3. **Multiply 818 by the hundreds place digit (800):**\n   \\[\n   818 \\times 800 = 654400\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(818 \\times 8 = 6544\\), then add two zeros (since 800 is \\(8 \\times 100\\)).\n   - Result: 654400.\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   6544 + 8180 + 654400\n   \\]\n   - First, add 6544 and 8180:\n     \\[\n     6544 + 8180 = 14724\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to 654400:\n     \\[\n     14724 + 654400 = 669124\n     \\]\n\nVerification using the algebraic expansion \\((a + b)^2 = a^2 + 2ab + b^2\\) where \\(a = 800\\) and \\(b = 18\\):\n   - \\(800^2 = 640000\\)\n   - \\(2 \\times 800 \\times 18 = 28800\\)\n   - \\(18^2 = 324\\)\n   - Summing these: \\(640000 + 28800 + 324 = 669124\\)\n\nThus, the final product of 818 and 818 is \\(\\boxed{669124}\\).",
