 exactly what I did. So that's correct.\n\nNow, I need to add all three results together: 5,236 (from the ones place) + 67,320 (from the tens place) + 598,400 (from the hundreds place). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 5,236 + 67,320. Adding those: 5,236 + 60,000 is 65,236. Then add 7,320 more: 65,236 +7,320 = 72,556. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Wait, maybe I should add them properly. 5,236 +67,320. Let's line them up:.\n\n  5,236.\n+67,320.\n--------.\n 72,556? Hmm, yes, because 5k +67k is 72k, and 236 +320 is 556. So that's correct.\n\nNow add the third number: 72,556 +598,400. Let's see, 72,556 + 598,400</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
