 that might complicate, but let's see:\n\nFirst, 400*300 = 120,000\n\n400*30 =12,000\n\n400*6 =2,400\n\n50*300=15,000\n\n50*30=1,500\n\n50*6=300\n\n3*300=900\n\n3*30=90\n\n3*6=18\n\nNow add all these up:\n\nStart with 120,000\n\n+12,000 \u2192132,000\n\n+2,400 \u2192134,400\n\n+15,000 \u2192149,400\n\n+1,500 \u2192150,900\n\n+300 \u2192151,200\n\n+900 \u2192152,100\n\n+90 \u2192152,190\n\n+18 \u2192152,208.\n\nYes, same result. So that confirms it. Therefore, the product is 152,208. Okay, so the step-by-step breakdown was correct. I think that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 453 and 336 is \\boxed{152208}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 453 and 336?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 336 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 453 by the ones place digit 6 of 336:\n   \\[\n   453 \\times 6 = 2718\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 453 by the tens place digit 30 of 336:\n   \\[\n   453 \\times 30 = 13590\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 453 by the hundreds place digit 300 of 336:\n   \\[\n   453 \\times 300 = 135900\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n2718 + 13590 + 135900 = 152208\n\\]\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 2718 + 13590 + 135900 = 152208.\nSo, the final computed product is 152208.\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{152208}\n\\]",
