0 = 27,000\n\n30\u00d770 = 2,100\n\n30\u00d76 = 180\n\nNow add all those together:\n\n450,000 + 35,000 = 485,000\n\n485,000 + 3,000 = 488,000\n\n488,000 + 27,000 = 515,000\n\n515,000 + 2,100 = 517,100\n\n517,100 + 180 = 517,280. Yep, same result. So that's correct.\n\nAlright, so all methods confirm that the product is 517,280.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 530 and 976 is \\boxed{517280}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 530 and 976, we break down 976 into its place values and multiply each part by 530, then sum the results.\n\n1. **Multiply 530 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   530 \\times 6 = 3180\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 530 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   530 \\times 70 = 530 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 3710 \\times 10 = 37100\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 530 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   530 \\times 900 = 530 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 4770 \\times 100 = 477000\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the results:**\n\\[\n3180 + 37100 + 477000 = 40280 + 477000 = 517280\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 530 and 976 is \\(\\boxed{517280}\\).",
