eds place, it's already in the correct position (shifted two places to the left from the original number).\n\nNow I have to add all three results together: 7208 (from the ones), 27,030 (from the tens), and 180,200 (from the hundreds). Let me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, add 7208 and 27,030. Let's see, 7208 + 27,030. Adding the thousands: 7,000 + 27,000 is 34,000. Then the hundreds, tens, and ones: 208 + 30 is 238. So total so far is 34,000 + 238 = 34,238.\n\nNow add that to 180,200. So 34,238 + 180,200. Breaking it down, 34,000 + 180,000 is 214,000. Then 238 + 200 is 438</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
