ts of 490 (which is 400 + 90 + 0):\n\n1. **Multiply 109 by the ones place digit (0):**\n   \\[\n   109 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 109 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   109 \\times 90 = 109 \\times 9 \\times 10 = 981 \\times 10 = 9810\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 109 by the hundreds place digit (400):**\n   \\[\n   109 \\times 400 = 109 \\times 4 \\times 100 = 436 \\times 100 = 43600\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the step results:**\n\\[\n0 + 9810 + 43600 = 53410\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 109 and 490 is \\(\\boxed{53410}\\).", '']
