1416. Multiply by 100 gives 141,600. .\n\nNow, add all three partial products together: 2478 + 28,320 + 141,600. Let me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 2478 + 28,320. Let's see, 2478 + 28,000 = 30,478. Then add the remaining 320: 30,478 + 320 = 30,798.\n\nNow add that to 141,600. 30,798 + 141,600. Hmm, 30,000 + 141,600 = 171,600</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
