e estimation is okay. Alternatively, 262×526 ≈ 260×530 = 137,800, which is very close to 137,812. So that seems plausible. I think the calculation is correct. So the final answer is 137,812.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 262 and 526 is \\boxed{137812}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 262 and 526?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 526 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places.\n1. Multiply 262 by the ones place digit (6) of 526:\n   \\[\n   262 \\times 6 = 1572\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 262 by the tens place digit (20) of 526:\n   \\[\n   262 \\times 20 = 5240\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 262 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 526:\n   \\[\n   262 \\times 500 = 131000\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1572 + 5240 + 131000 = 137812\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{137812}.", '']
