 +368,500:\n\nTake 72,963 + 300,000 = 372,963\n\nThen add 68,500 to that: 372,963 +68,500. Let's see:\n\n372,963 +60,000 =432,963\n\nThen add 8,500: 432,963 +8,500 =441,463. Wait, so total would be 441,463?\n\nWait, now I'm confused. Wait, 368,500 is 300k +68,500. So 72,963 + 300,000 is 372,963. Then adding the remaining 68,500 to that gives 372,963 +68,500. Let me compute that again:\n\n372,963 +68,500:\n\nAdd 372,963 +60,000 =432,963\n\nThen add 8,500: 432,963 +8,500 =441,463. So total is 441,463?\n\nWait, but earlier when I added digit by digit, I got 741,463. Which is conflicting. Hmm, so I must have messed up in one of the steps.\n\nWait, perhaps I made an error in the first addition step. Let me recalculate 6,633 +66,330.\n\n6,633 +66,330:\n\n6,000 +66,000 =72,000\n\n633 + 330 = 963\n\nTotal is 72,000 +963 =72,963. That's correct.\n\nThen adding to 368,500:\n\n72,963 +368,500. Let me write both numbers:\n\n72,963\n\n+368,500\n\nAlign properly:\n\n72,963\n\n+368,500\n\n------------\n\nAdding:\n\nUnits place: 3+0=3\n\nTens:6+0=6\n\nHundreds:9+5=14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nThousands:2 +8=10 plus the 1 is 11. Write 1, carryover 1.\n\nTen-thousands:7 +6=13 plus 1 is 14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nHundred-thousands: 0 (from first number) +3 (from second number) plus the 1 carried over is 4. So the total is 441,463.\n\nWait, so where did I get 741,463 before? Oh, I see! I must have added the numbers incorrectly in the first digit-by-digit approach. Let me try again:\n\nThe first number is 72,963 (which is 072,963 if considering 6 digits)\n\nThe second number is 368,500.\n\nAdding:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n3 (units) +0 =3\n\n6 (tens) +0=6\n\n9 (hundreds) +5 (hundreds) =14, write 4, carryover 1\n\n2 (thousands place of first number) +8 (thousands place of second number) =10, plus the 1 carried over is 11. So write 1, carryover 1.\n\n7 (ten-thousands place of first number) +6 (ten-thousands of second number) =13, plus 1 =14. Write 4, carryover 1.\n\nNow, the hundred thousands place: the first number has 0 (since it's 072,963), the second has 3, plus the carryover 1 gives 4.\n\nSo the total is 441,463. So that's correct. Earlier, when I thought I had 741,463, I must have added the hundred thousands digits wrong by adding 3+3 instead of 0+3. Because the first number is 72,963, which is only 5 digits, so the hundred thousands place is 0. So that was my mistake.\n\nSo the correct total is 441,463. Wait, but let me check with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps I can use the standard algorithm for multiplying 737 ×599 directly.\n\nLet me write it out:\n\n       737\n\n     ×599\n\n     ---------\n\nFirst, multiply 737 by 9 (the ones place):\n\n737×9 = 6,633.\n\nThen multiply 737 by 90 (the tens place, which is 9×10):\n\n737×90 = 66,330.\n\nThen multiply 737 by 500 (the hundreds place, 5×100):\n\n737×500 = 368,500.\n\nNow add them all together:\n\n6,633\n\n+66,330\n\n=72,963\n\nThen 72,963 +368,500 =441,463.\n\nHmm, so that's consistent. So the final answer should be 441,463.\n\nWait, but let me verify with another approach to be absolutely sure. Maybe using the distributive property:\n\n737 × 599 = 737 × (600 -1) = 737×600 -737×1.\n\nCalculating that:\n\n737 ×600 = 442,200 (since 737×6=4,422, so ×100 is 442,200)\n\nThen subtract 737×1 =737.\n\nSo 442,200 -737 = ?\n\n442,200 - 700 =441,500\n\nThen subtract 37 more: 441,500 -37 =441,463.\n\nYes! That matches. So that confirms it's 441,463.\n\nTherefore, the initial mistake in my first addition was a miscalculation when I thought I had 741,463, but that was an error in adding the hundred thousands place. So the correct total is 441,463.\n\nSo the steps are correct, and the final answer is 441,463. I think that's solid now. Let me just recap the reasoning as per the template.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 737 and 599 is \\boxed{441463}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 737 and 599?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 599 has three digits, so we can break it down into hundreds, tens, and ones places:\n1. Multiply 737 by the ones place digit 9 of 599:\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 9 = 6,\\!633\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 737 by the tens place digit 90 (which is \\(9 \\times 10\\)) of 599:\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 90 = 66,\\!330\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 737 by the hundreds place digit 500 (which is \\(5 \\times 100\\)) of 599:\n   \\[\n   737 \\times 500 = 368,\\!500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n6,\\!633 + 66,\\!330 + 368,\\!500 = 441,\\!463\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is 441,463.\n\n### Answer:\nThe product of 737 and 599 is \\boxed{441463}.", '']
