0 (tens place) = 28,800\n\n3. Multiply 720 by 300 (hundreds place) = 216,000\n\nSum: 5,760 + 28,800 + 216,000 = 250,560\n\nSo the final answer is 250,560.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 720 and 348 is \\boxed{250560}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 720 and 348, we break down the multiplication step by step using the place values of the digits in 348:\n\n1. **Multiply 720 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 8 = 5760\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 720 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 40 = 720 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 2880 \\times 10 = 28800\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 720 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   720 \\times 300 = 720 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 2160 \\times 100 = 216000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results from the steps above:\n\\[\n5760 + 28800 + 216000 = 250560\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 720 and 348 is \\(\\boxed{250560}\\).", '']
