(because 350*7=2,450 and 3*7=21; adding those gives 2,471). Then multiply by 100 to get 700. So 2,471 *100 is 247,100. That seems right.\n\nNow I have to add all three results together: 1765 (from ones) + 17,650 (from tens) + 247,100 (from hundreds). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, 1765 + 17,650. Let's see: 1765 + 17,650. Adding the thousands: 17,650 is 17 thousand, and 1,765 is 1 thousand 765. So total thousands would be 19, and then the remaining 765? Wait, no, actually 17,650 + 1,000 is 18,650, plus 765 more. 18,650 + 700 is 19,350, plus 65 is 19,415. Wait, maybe another way: 17,650 + 1,765. Let me add 17,650 + 1,700 first, which is 19,350, then add 65 more: 19,415. .\n\nThen add that to 247,100. So 19,415 + 247,100. Let's see: 247,100 + 19,415. Adding the thousands: 247,100 + 10,000 is 257,100, then add 9,415</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
