 Let's see, 188 is 200 -12. So 549*(200 -12) = 549*200 -549*12.\n\n549*200 = 109,800.\n\n549*12: 549*10=5,490; 549*2=1,098. So total 5,490 +1,098=6,588.\n\nSubtract: 109,800 -6,588 = ?\n\n109,800 - 6,000 = 103,800.\n\nThen subtract 588 more: 103,800 -588 = 103,212. So that's the same answer. \n\nOkay, so that confirms it again. So the product is indeed 103,212. I think that's correct. I don't see any errors in my steps.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 188 and 549?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 549 has three digits, so we break it into ones, tens, and hundreds places.  \n1. **Multiply 188 by the ones place (9):**  \n   \\( 188 \\times 9 = 1,\\!692 \\).  \n2. **Multiply 188 by the tens place (40):**  \n   \\( 188 \\times 40 = 7,\\!520 \\).  \n3. **Multiply 188 by the hundreds place (500):**  \n   \\( 188 \\times 500 = 94,\\!000 \\).  \n\n**Sum all the step results:**  \n\\( 1,\\!692 + 7,\\!520 = 9,\\!212 \\), then \\( 9,\\!212 + 94,\\!000 = 103,\\!212 \\).  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\( 1,\\!692 + 7,\\!520 + 94,\\!000 = 103,\\!212 \\).  \nSo, the final computed product is **103,212**.",
