.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 337,851.\n\nWait, but in my initial steps, when I added the first two partial products (6111 +69840=75,951), then adding to 261,900 gives 337,851, which is correct. So I think that's the right answer.\n\nSo putting it into the template:\n\nThe product of 873 and 387 is calculated by breaking down the multiplication into three steps based on the digits of 387:\n\n1. Multiply 873 by 7 (the ones place): 873 \u00d7 7 = 6,111.\n2. Multiply 873 by 80 (the tens place): 873 \u00d7 80 = 69,840.\n3. Multiply 873 by 300 (the hundreds place): 873 \u00d7 300 = 261,900.\n\nAdding all these results together: 6,111 + 69,840 + 261,900 = 337,851.\n\nSo the final product is 337,851.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 873 and 387 is \\boxed{337851}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 873 and 387, we break down the multiplication into three steps based on the digits of 387:\n\n1. **Multiply 873 by 7 (the ones place):**\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 7 = 6111\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 873 by 80 (the tens place):**\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 80 = 69840\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 873 by 300 (the hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   873 \\times 300 = 261900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the results of these partial products:\n\\[\n6111 + 69840 + 261900 = 337851\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 873 and 387 is \\(\\boxed{337851}\\).",
