:\n\nStart with 894 × 9 = 8,046\n\nThen 894 × 1 (tens place) = 894, but shifted one position to the left: 8,940\n\nThen 894 ×7 (hundreds place) = 6,258, shifted two positions: 625,800\n\nAdding them: 8,046 + 8,940 = 16,986; then 16,986 + 625,800 = 642,786. Yep, same result.\n\nI think that's correct. Let me just check with a calculator-like approach.\n\nAlternatively, compute 894 × 700 = 625,800. Then 894 ×19 = ?\n\nWait, 894 × 20 = 17,880, minus 894 gives 17,880 - 894 = 16,986. Then total is 625,800 +16,986 = 642,786. Yep.\n\nAlternatively, compute 800×700 = 560,000; 800×10=8,000; 800×9=7,200; then 90×700=63,000; 90×10=900; 90×9=810; 4×700=2,800; 4×10=40; 4×9=36. Wait, but this is breaking it into all components, which might be too tedious, but let me try:\n\nWait, maybe that's overcomplicating. Alternatively, since all methods so far give 642,786, I can be confident that's the correct answer. I don't see any arithmetic errors in my steps. So the final product should be 642,786.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 894 and 719 is \\boxed{642786}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 894 and 719, we use the standard multiplication method by breaking it down into partial products and then summing them up.\n\n1. **Multiply 894 by the ones place digit (9) of 719:**\n   \\[\n   894 \\times 9 = 8046\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(800 \\times 9 = 7200\\), \\(90 \\times 9 = 810\\), \\(4 \\times 9 = 36\\)\n   - Sum: \\(7200 + 810 + 36 = 8046\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 894 by the tens place digit (10) of 719:**\n   \\[\n   894 \\times 10 = 8940\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 894 by the hundreds place digit (700) of 719:**\n   \\[\n   894 \\times 700 = 625800\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(894 \\times 7 = 6258\\), then multiply by 100: \\(6258 \\times 100 = 625800\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   8046 + 8940 + 625800\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(8046\\) and \\(8940\\):\n     \\[\n     8046 + 8940 = 16986\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(625800\\):\n     \\[\n     625800 + 16986 = 642786\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 894 and 719 is \\(\\boxed{642786}\\).", '']
