 three digits. Here, 775 is three digits (hundreds, tens, ones), so three steps as well. The first step is multiplying by the ones digit (5), second by the tens digit (70), third by the hundreds digit (700). Then sum all three.\n\nSo the answer is 290,625. Got it. I think that's solid now. Just need to format it into the template correctly.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 375 and 775 is \\boxed{290625}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 375 and 775?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 775 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 375 by the ones place digit (5) of 775:\n   \\[\n   375 \\times 5 = 1875\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 375 by the tens place digit (70) of 775:\n   \\[\n   375 \\times 70 = 26250\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 375 by the hundreds place digit (700) of 775:\n   \\[\n   375 \\times 700 = 262500\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n1875 + 26250 + 262500 = 290625\n\\]\n\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: 1875 + 26250 + 262500 = 290625.\n\nSo, the final computed product is 290625.\n\n### Final Answer\nThe product of 375 and 775 is \\boxed{290625}.", '']
