      "text": "76,804? Wait, let me check that again. 72,800 plus 4,004.\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n72,800 + 4,000 =76,800.\n\nThen add the remaining 4: 76,800 +4 =76,804. Yes, that's correct.\n\nWait a second, but let me confirm using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake. Maybe multiply directly?\n\nAlternatively, 364 \u00d7211. Let's do it the standard multiplication way:\n\nFirst, write 364\n\n\u00d7211\n\n------------\n\nMultiply 364 by 1 (units place): 364.\n\nMultiply 364 by 1 (tens place, so actually 10): 3640 shifted one position.\n\nMultiply 364 by 2 (hundreds place, so 200): 728 shifted two positions.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n\u202f\u00a0364\n\n\u00d7211\n\n\u202f\u00a0\u2014\u2014\n\n\u202f\u00a0364 (364\u00d71)\n\n+3640 (364\u00d710)\n\n+72800 (364\u00d7200)\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nTotal is 364 +3640 = 4004; then 4004 +72,800 = 76,804. So that's the same as before.\n\nHmm, so the answer should be 76,804. But let me check with another approach, perhaps using distributive property:\n\n364 \u00d7211 = 364 \u00d7(200 +10 +1) = 364\u00d7200 + 364\u00d710 +364\u00d71 = same as above. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using another method like breaking down 211 into 200 +11, but that might complicate.\n\nAlternatively, 364 \u00d7211 = 364 \u00d7 (200 +11) = 364\u00d7200 +364\u00d711. Let me see:\n\n364\u00d7200 is still 72,800.\n\n364\u00d711 is 364\u00d710 +364\u00d71=3,640 +364= 4,004.\n\nAdding those gives 72,800 +4,004 =76,804. Same result.\n\nHmm, seems consistent. Let me try using another method to cross-verify. Maybe the lattice method or something else? Maybe approximate?\n\nWell, 364 is approximately 360, and 211 is approximately 200. So 360\u00d7200=72,000. The actual answer should be a bit higher, which 76,804 is, so that makes sense.\n\nAlternatively, exact calculation:\n\nLet me do 364 \u00d7211 step by step again:\n\nFirst, write down:\n\n\u202f\u202f\u202f364\n\n\u00d7 211\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nMultiply 364 by 1 (the ones digit):\n\n364 \u00d71 = 364.\n\nMultiply 364 by 1 (the tens digit, which is actually 10):\n\n364 \u00d710 = 3640. So we write this shifted one position to the left.\n\nMultiply 364 by 2 (the hundreds digit, which is 200):\n\n364 \u00d7200 = 72,800. Shifted two positions to the left.\n\nNow adding them:\n\n364\n\n3640\n\n72800\n\nAdding the first two: 364 + 3640 = 4004.\n\nThen 4004 +72800 = 76804. Yes, same result.\n\nTherefore, I think the product is 76,804. I don't see any errors in the steps. Let me check once more with a calculator approach, but since I can't use a calculator, maybe breaking down the numbers differently?\n\nAlternatively, 211 is 200 +11. So 364\u00d7200 =72,800 and 364\u00d711=4,004. Adding those gives 76,804. Yep, same.\n\nAlternatively, 364 \u00d7211 can be thought as 364\u00d7(200 +10 +1) = same as above.\n\nAlternatively, using the distributive property another way: 364 \u00d7211 = (300 +60 +4) \u00d7211 = 300\u00d7211 +60\u00d7211 +4\u00d7211.\n\nLet me compute each part:\n\n300\u00d7211 = 300\u00d7200 +300\u00d711 =60,000 +3,300 =63,300.\n\n60\u00d7211 = 60\u00d7200 +60\u00d711 =12,000 +660 =12,660.\n\n4\u00d7211 = 844.\n\nAdding those together: 63,300 +12,660 =75,960; then +844 gives 76,804. Yep, same answer.\n\nAlright, so all methods lead to 76,804. I think that's correct. So the final answer should be 76,804.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 364 and 211 is \\boxed{76804}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 364 and 211?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 211 has three digits, so we can break it down into its place values:\n1. Multiply 364 by 1 (the ones place of 211): \n   \\[\n   364 \\times 1 = 364\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 364 by 10 (the tens place of 211):\n   \\[\n   364 \\times 10 = 3640\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 364 by 200 (the hundreds place of 211):\n   \\[\n   364 \\times 200 = 72800\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n364 + 3640 + 72800 = 76804\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{76804}.",
