's the right answer after verifying through multiple methods.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 524 and 780 is \\boxed{408720}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 524 and 780?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 780 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps based on place value.\n1. Multiply 524 by the ones place digit 0 of 780:  \n   \\(524 \\times 0 = 0\\)\n2. Multiply 524 by the tens place digit 80 of 780:  \n   \\(524 \\times 80 = 41,920\\)\n3. Multiply 524 by the hundreds place digit 700 of 780:  \n   \\(524 \\times 700 = 366,800\\)\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(0 + 41,920 + 366,800 = 408,720\\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{408720}.",
