ing another multiplication approach, like the distributive property.\n\n444 \u00d7 981 can be written as 444 \u00d7 (900 + 80 + 1) = 444\u00d7900 + 444\u00d780 + 444\u00d71, which is exactly what I did. So the components are correct. The sum of those components must be correct if each part is right. So 399,600 + 35,520 = 435,120. Then adding 444 gives 435,564. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can do the multiplication directly.\n\nLet me try multiplying 444 by 981 the standard way:\n\n```\n      444  \n    \u00d7981  \n    -------\n```\n\nStarting with multiplying by the ones digit (1):\n\n444 \u00d7 1 = 444.\n\nThen multiplying by the tens digit (8), but shifted one position to the left (equivalent to \u00d710):\n\n444 \u00d78 = 3,552; written as 35,520.\n\nThen multiplying by the hundreds digit (9), shifted two positions (equivalent to \u00d7100):\n\n444 \u00d79 = 3,996; written as 399,600.\n\nAdding them up:\n\n444  \n35,520  \n399,600  \n----------\nTotal: 444 + 35,520 = 35,964; 35,964 + 399,600 = 435,564. \n\nYes, that matches. So the correct total is 435,564. \n\nWait a minute, but when I first thought of the answer, I might have miscalculated the addition steps. But after verifying, it's clear that the total is 435,564. \n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method, like the difference of squares or some other trick, but with these numbers it might not be straightforward. Alternatively, let me check using a calculator approach:\n\n444 \u00d7 981. Let's compute 444 \u00d7 1000 first, which is 444,000. Then subtract 444 \u00d7 19 (since 1000 - 19 = 981). Wait, 981 = 1000 - 19. \n\nSo 444 \u00d7 981 = 444\u00d7(1000 - 19) = 444,000 - (444\u00d719).\n\nCompute 444 \u00d719: 444\u00d720 = 8,880 minus 444 gives 8,880 -444 = 8,436.\n\nThus, 444,000 - 8,436 = 435,564. \n\nYes! That confirms it again. So the answer is indeed 435,564. \n\nSo my initial steps were correct, but I had to make sure the addition was done properly. The key was breaking it down step by step and