ted one position to the left (since it's the tens place):\n\n841 \u00d76 = 5,046, so shifted becomes 50,460.\n\nThen the hundreds digit (7), shifted two positions to the left (hundreds place):\n\n841 \u00d77 =5,887, shifted two becomes 588,700.\n\nAdding those three gives the same total as before. So that's correct.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps use a calculator check? Since I can't use a calculator, but maybe approximate to see if it's reasonable.\n\n800 \u00d7700 = 560,000.\n\n800\u00d760=48,000; 800\u00d74=3,200. So 560k +48k=608k +3.2k=611,200.\n\nThen the remaining 41\u00d7764: 41\u00d7700=28,700; 41\u00d760=2,460; 41\u00d74=164. Adding those: 28,700+2,460=31,160 +164=31,324.\n\nTotal would be 611,200 +31,324=642,524. Exactly the same. So that cross-verification works.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the product is 642,524.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 841 and 764 is \\boxed{642524}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 841 and 764?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 764 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 841 by the ones place digit 4 of 764:\n   \\[\n   841 \\times 4 = 3364\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 841 by the tens place digit 60 of 764:\n   \\[\n   841 \\times 60 = 50460\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 841 by the hundreds place digit 700 of 764:\n   \\[\n   841 \\times 700 = 588700\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n3364 + 50460 + 588700 = 642524\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{642524}.",
