1400+140=1540. Then multiply by 10 gives 15,400. So that's the second step result.\n\n3. Now the hundreds place digit. The hundreds digit is 7, which is actually 700. So 220 × 700. Let's see, 220 ×7 is 1540 again, so times 100 would be 1540×100 = 154,000. So that's the third step result.\n\nNow, adding all three results together: 1,320 (from ones) + 15,400 (tens) + 154,000 (hundreds). Let me add them step by step.\n\nFirst, 1,320 + 15,400. Let's see, 1,320 +15,000 is 16,320, then add 400 more to get 16,720. Then add that to 154,000. 154,000 + 16,720</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
