20 by the tens place digit (70):\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 70 = 15400\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 220 by the hundreds place digit (700):\n   \\[\n   220 \\times 700 = 154000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n1320 + 15400 + 154000\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n- First, add 1320 and 15400:\n  \\[\n  1320 + 15400 = 16720\n  \\]\n- Then add the result to 154000:\n  \\[\n  16720 + 154000 = 170720\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 220 and 776 is \\(\\boxed{170720}\\).", '']
