e place values of 911 (hundreds, tens, and ones):\n\n1. **Multiply 424 by the ones place digit (1):**\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 1 = 424\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 424 by the tens place digit (10):**\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 10 = 4240\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 424 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 900 = 424 \\times 9 \\times 100\n   \\]\n   First, calculate \\(424 \\times 9\\):\n   \\[\n   424 \\times 9 = 3816\n   \\]\n   Then multiply by 100:\n   \\[\n   3816 \\times 100 = 381600\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the results:**\n\\[\n424 + 4240 + 381600\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n\\[\n424 + 4240 = 4664\n\\]\n\\[\n4664 + 381600 = 386264\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 424 and 911 is \\(\\boxed{386264}\\).",
