0\n\nNow, adding all these:\n\n90,000 + 36,000 = 126,000\n\n126,000 +5,400 = 131,400\n\n131,400 +500 = 131,900\n\n131,900 +200 = 132,100\n\n132,100 +30 = 132,130.\n\nSame answer again. So, definitely, the product is 132,130. I think that's solid. So the answer is 132,130.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 905 and 146 is \\boxed{132130}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 905 and 146, we break down the multiplication step by step using the place values of 146:\n\n1. **Multiply 905 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   905 \\times 6 = 5430\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 905 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   905 \\times 40 = 905 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3620 \\times 10 = 36200\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 905 by the hundreds place digit (100):**\n   \\[\n   905 \\times 100 = 90500\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n5430 + 36200 + 90500\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n- First, add \\(5430\\) and \\(36200\\):\n  \\[\n  5430 + 36200 = 41630\n  \\]\n\n- Then add the result to \\(90500\\):\n  \\[\n  41630 + 90500 = 132130\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{132130}\\).",
