initial step-by-step multiplication, the partial products were right.\n\nFirst partial product: 606\u00d77=4,242. Correct.\n\nSecond: 606\u00d79 (tens place, so 90) \u2192 606\u00d79=5,454, then shifted one position becomes 54,540. Correct.\n\nThird: 606\u00d77 (hundreds place, so 700) \u2192 606\u00d77=4,242, shifted two positions becomes 424,200. Correct.\n\nAdding them: 4,242 +54,540 =58,782; then 58,782 +424,200=482,982. All steps check out. So the answer is 482,982.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 606 and 797 is \\boxed{482982}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 606 and 797, we break it down into steps using the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\n1. **Multiply 606 by the ones place digit (7):**\n   \\[\n   606 \\times 7 = 4242\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 606 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   606 \\times 9 = 5454 \\quad \\text{(then shift one position left)} \\quad \\rightarrow 54540\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 606 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   606 \\times 7 = 4242 \\quad \\text{(then shift two positions left)} \\quad \\rightarrow 424200\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the partial results:**\n   \\[\n   4242 + 54540 + 424200\n   \\]\n\n   - Adding the first two partial products:\n     \\[\n     4242 + 54540 = 58782\n     \\]\n   - Adding the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     58782 + 424200 = 482982\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 606 and 797 is \\(\\boxed{482982}\\).",
