5,400 -9,900 = 635,500.\n\n635,500 -242 = 635,258. So same answer. That's a good check.\n\nHmm, so that matches. So 635,258 is correct.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use calculator-like step-by-step multiplication:\n\nMultiply 689 \u00d7 922.\n\nLet me write it vertically:\n\n      689\n\n    \u00d7922\n\n    --------\n\nFirst, multiply 689 by 2 (units digit):\n\n689 \u00d72 =1,378.\n\nThen multiply 689 by 20 (tens digit, so shift one position):\n\n689 \u00d720=13,780.\n\nThen multiply 689 by 900 (hundreds digit, shift two positions):\n\n689 \u00d7900=620,100.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n1,378\n\n13,780\n\n620,100\n\nAdding first two gives 15,158, plus 620,100 gives 635,258.\n\nAlright, so all methods lead to the same result. Therefore, the product of 689 and 922 is 635,258.\n\nBut wait, let me just confirm with another cross-verification. Let me compute 689 \u00d7 900 = 620,100. Then 689 \u00d722 = ?\n\n689 \u00d722 = 689\u00d7(20+2)=13,780 +1,378=15,158. Then adding to 620,100 gives 635,258. Yep, same thing.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use estimation to check if the answer is reasonable.\n\n689 is approximately 700, and 922 is approximately 900. 700\u00d7900=630,000. The actual numbers are slightly less: 689 is 11 less than 700, and 922 is 22 more than 900. So the exact value would be 700\u00d7900 minus 11\u00d7900 plus 700\u00d722 minus 11\u00d722, but that's similar to the earlier method. Anyway, the approximate is 630k, and the exact is 635k, which makes sense. So that seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do a quick division check: if 635,258 divided by 689 should give 922.\n\nLet me try that division: 635,258 \u00f7689.\n\nFirst, 689 \u00d7900=620,100. Subtract that from 635,258: 635,258 -620,100 =15,158.\n\nNow, 689 \u00d722 =15,158. So adding 900 +22 gives 922. So yes, that works. Therefore, division checks out.\n\nTherefore, I'm confident the answer is correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 689 and 922 is \\boxed{635258}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 689