n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 949 and 786 is \\boxed{745914}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 949 and 786, we break it down into three steps based on the digits of 786:\n\n1. **Multiply 949 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 6 = 5694\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(9 \\times 6 = 54\\), write 4, carry over 5.\n   - \\(4 \\times 6 + 5 = 29\\), write 9, carry over 2.\n   - \\(9 \\times 6 + 2 = 56\\), write 56.\n\n2. **Multiply 949 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 80 = 75920\n   \\]\n   - First, calculate \\(949 \\times 8 = 7592\\).\n   - Then add a zero: \\(7592 \\times 10 = 75920\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 949 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   949 \\times 700 = 664300\n   \\]\n   - First, calculate \\(949 \\times 7 = 6643\\).\n   - Then add two zeros: \\(6643 \\times 100 = 664300\\).\n\n**Summing all the results:**\n\\[\n5694 + 75920 + 664300\n\\]\n- Add \\(5694\\) and \\(75920\\):\n  \\[\n  5694 + 75920 = 81614\n  \\]\n- Add the result to \\(664300\\):\n  \\[\n  81614 + 664300 = 745914\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final product of 949 and 786 is \\(\\boxed{745914}\\).",
