ply each term:\n\nFirst, 600\u00d7700 =420,000\n\n600\u00d720 =12,000\n\n600\u00d73=1,800\n\nThen 60\u00d7700 =42,000\n\n60\u00d720=1,200\n\n60\u00d73=180\n\nThen 1\u00d7700=700\n\n1\u00d720=20\n\n1\u00d73=3\n\nNow add all those up:\n\n420,000\n\n+12,000 \u2192 432,000\n\n+1,800 \u2192 433,800\n\n+42,000 \u2192 475,800\n\n+1,200 \u2192477,000\n\n+180 \u2192477,180\n\n+700 \u2192477,880\n\n+20 \u2192477,900\n\n+3 \u2192477,903.\n\nYes, same result. So that must be correct. Therefore, the product of 661 and 723 is 477,903.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me use a calculator approach. Let me compute 661 \u00d7723:\n\n661 \u00d7700 = 462,700\n\n661 \u00d723 = ?\n\n661 \u00d720 =13,220\n\n661 \u00d73 =1,983\n\nSo 13,220 +1,983 =15,203\n\nThen total is 462,700 +15,203 =477,903. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nAlright, so all methods lead to 477,903. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 661 and 723 is \\boxed{477903}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 661 and 723?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 723 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps based on place value:\n1. Multiply 661 by the ones place digit 3:  \n   \\(661 \\times 3 = 1983\\)\n2. Multiply 661 by the tens place digit 20:  \n   \\(661 \\times 20 = 13220\\)\n3. Multiply 661 by the hundreds place digit 700:  \n   \\(661 \\times 700 = 462700\\)\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(1983 + 13220 + 462700 = 477903\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{477903}.",
