 50%|####9     | 249/500 [3:07:05<3:32:54, 50.90s/it]["477,700 plus 203 more. 477,700 + 200 is 477,900, then +3 is 477,903. Wait, that doesn't seem right. Wait, maybe I messed up the addition steps.\n\nWait, let me recalculate:\n\nFirst step: 661 *3 = 1983\n\nSecond step: 661*20 = 13,220\n\nThird step: 661*700 = 462,700\n\nNow adding all three:\n\nStart with 1983 + 13,220 = ?\n\n1983 + 13,220: 13,220 + 1,983.\n\n13,220 + 1,000 =14,220\n\n14,220 + 983 = 15,203. So that part is correct.\n\nThen 15,203 + 462,700.\n\nAdding 15,203 to 462,700:\n\n462,700 + 15,203.\n\nLet me add the thousands first: 462,700 + 15,000 = 477,700.\n\nThen add the remaining 203: 477,700 +203 = 477,903.\n\nHmm, so the total would be 477,903?\n\nWait a second, let me verify using another method to ensure I didn't make a mistake.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should do the multiplication the standard way:\n\n   661\n\nx723\n\n--------\n\nFirst multiply 661 by 3: 1983\n\nThen multiply 661 by 20 (shift one position): 13,220\n\nThen multiply 661 by 700 (shift two positions): 462,700\n\nAdding those three gives the total. So yes, that's the same as before.\n\nWait, but when adding 1983 +13220 +462700:\n\nLet me do it another way:\n\n462,700\n\n+ 13,220 = 475,920\n\nThen +1,983 = 475,920 +1,983.\n\n475,920 + 1,000 =476,920\n\n476,920 + 983 =477,903. Same result.\n\nHmm. But let me check with another method, like the standard algorithm:\n\nMultiplying 661 × 723.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n      661\n\n    ×723\n\n    --------\n\nFirst step: 661 ×3 = 1983\n\nSecond step: 661 ×20 = 13,220 (written as shifted one position to the left)\n\nThird step: 661 ×700 = 462,700 (shifted two positions to the left)\n\nAdding all three:\n\n1983\n\n13220\n\n462700\n\nTotal:\n\nStart with units: 1983 +13220 =15203, then +462700 gives 477,903. So that seems correct.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another approach, maybe using the distributive property in another way.\n\nAlternatively, (600 +60 +1) × (700 +20 +3).\n\nMultiply each term:\n\nFirst, 600×700 =420,000\n\n600×20 =12,000\n\n600×3=1,800\n\nThen 60×700 =42,000\n\n60×20=1,200\n\n60×3=180\n\nThen 1×700=700\n\n1×20=20\n\n1×3=3\n\nNow add all those up:\n\n420,000\n\n+12,000 → 432,000\n\n+1,800 → 433,800\n\n+42,000 → 475,800\n\n+1,200 →477,000\n\n+180 →477,180\n\n+700 →477,880\n\n+20 →477,900\n\n+3 →477,903.\n\nYes, same result. So that must be correct. Therefore, the product of 661 and 723 is 477,903.\n\nWait, but just to be thorough, let me use a calculator approach. Let me compute 661 ×723:\n\n661 ×700 = 462,700\n\n661 ×23 = ?\n\n661 ×20 =13,220\n\n661 ×3 =1,983\n\nSo 13,220 +1,983 =15,203\n\nThen total is 462,700 +15,203 =477,903. Yep, that's consistent.\n\nAlright, so all methods lead to 477,903. I think that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 661 and 723 is \\boxed{477903}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 661 and 723?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. The number 723 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps based on place value:\n1. Multiply 661 by the ones place digit 3:  \n   \\(661 \\times 3 = 1983\\)\n2. Multiply 661 by the tens place digit 20:  \n   \\(661 \\times 20 = 13220\\)\n3. Multiply 661 by the hundreds place digit 700:  \n   \\(661 \\times 700 = 462700\\)\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(1983 + 13220 + 462700 = 477903\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{477903}.", '']
