    879300  (977 x 9, shifted two positions)\n    --------\n     918380\n\nYes, adding those:\n\nStart from the right:\n0 (units place)\n0 + 0 (tens place)\n8 (hundreds place) + 8 (from 39080's hundreds place) + 0 (from 879300's hundreds place, since it's shifted two places, so the hundreds digit would be the third from the right... Wait, maybe I need to align them properly.\n\nWait, actually, when written vertically:\n\nFirst partial product (0) is just 0.\n\nSecond partial product (40 place) is 39080 (so written as 39080).\n\nThird partial product (900 place) is 879300 (written as 879300).\n\nAdding them:\n\n   39080\n+879300\n--------\n  918380\n\nYes, that's correct. So all steps check out. I think that's the right answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 977 and 940 is \\boxed{918380}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 977 and 940, we break it down using the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. **Multiply 977 by the ones place digit (0) of 940:**\n   \\[\n   977 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 977 by the tens place digit (40) of 940:**\n   \\[\n   977 \\times 40 = 977 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 3908 \\times 10 = 39080\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 977 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 940:**\n   \\[\n   977 \\times 900 = 977 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 8793 \\times 100 = 879300\n   \\]\n\n**Sum all the step results:**\n\\[\n0 + 39080 + 879300 = 918380\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{918380}\\).", '']
