ace digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   327 \\times 80 = 327 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 2616 \\times 10 = 26160\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 327 by the hundreds place digit (800):**\n   \\[\n   327 \\times 800 = 327 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 2616 \\times 100 = 261600\n   \\]\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   654 + 26160 + 261600\n   \\]\n\n   - Adding the first two results:\n     \\[\n     654 + 26160 = 26814\n     \\]\n\n   - Adding the result to the third result:\n     \\[\n     26814 + 261600 = 288414\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{288414}\\).",
