rst:\n\n203 ×30 = 6,090\n\n203 ×7=1,421\n\nAdding those: 6,090 +1,421 =7,511. Then ×10 is 75,110.\n\nThen add 203×3=609, so total is 75,110 +609 =75,719. Yep, same result.\n\nAlright, so all methods lead to 75,719, so I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 203 and 373 is \\boxed{75719}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 203 and 373, we break it down step by step using the place values of 373 (ones, tens, and hundreds):\n\n1. **Multiply 203 by the ones place digit (3):**\n   \\[\n   203 \\times 3 = 609\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 203 by the tens place digit (70):**\n   \\[\n   203 \\times 70 = 203 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 1421 \\times 10 = 14210\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 203 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   203 \\times 300 = 203 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 609 \\times 100 = 60900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n609 + 14210 + 60900\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 609 and 14210:\n\\[\n609 + 14210 = 14819\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to 60900:\n\\[\n14819 + 60900 = 75719\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 203 and 373 is \\(\\boxed{75719}\\).", '']
