t me re-express the numbers:\n\n441600 is 441,600\n\n19,320 is 19,320\n\nAdding them:\n\nStart from the right:\n\nOnes place: 0 +0 =0\n\nTens place: 0 +2 =2\n\nHundreds place: 6 +3 =9\n\nThousands place: 1 +9 =10 \u2192 write 0, carryover 1\n\nTen thousands place: 4 (from first number) +1 (from second number's ten thousands place) plus the carried 1 \u2192 4+1+1=6\n\nWait, hold on. Wait, the thousands place: first number has 1 (thousands), second has 9 (thousands). So 1+9=10. So carryover 1 to the ten thousands.\n\nNow the ten thousands place: first number has 4 (ten thousands), second has 1 (ten thousands). So 4 +1 =5, plus the carried over 1 from thousands? Wait, no. Wait, the carryover from thousands is 1, which goes to the ten thousands place. So the ten thousands place calculation is 4 (original) +1 (from second number) +1 (carryover) =6.\n\nAh, here was the mistake! I forgot to add the carryover to the ten thousands place. So:\n\nTen thousands place becomes 4 (from first) +1 (from second) +1 (carryover) =6.\n\nThen the hundred thousands place: 4 (from first number) +0 (from second) =4.\n\nSo the digits are:\n\nHundred thousands:4\n\nTen thousands:6\n\nThousands:0 (from the 10 in thousands place)\n\nHundreds:9 (but wait, earlier I thought hundreds place was 6+3=9, but no carryover? Wait, let's recheck:\n\nWait, the hundreds place: first number's hundreds digit is 6, second is 3. So 6+3=9, no carryover. So hundreds is 9. Wait, but in the previous digit-wise addition I had written 0 there because I thought there was a carryover from thousands. Wait, no, the hundreds place is separate. Let me go step by step again.\n\nLet me do this carefully:\n\nNumber 1: 441,600\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- Hundred thousands: 4\n\n- Ten thousands:4\n\n- Thousands:1\n\n- Hundreds:6\n\n- Tens:0\n\n- Ones:0\n\nNumber 2: 19,320\n\nBreakdown:\n\n- Hundred thousands:0\n\n- Ten thousands:1\n\n- Thousands:9\n\n- Hundreds:3\n\n- Tens:2\n\n- Ones:0\n\nAdding digit by digit:\n\nOnes: 0 +0=0\n\nTens: