times 5 = 15 + 1 = 16\\)\n   - Multiply by 10: \\(1656 \\times 10 = 16560\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 552 by the hundreds place digit (800):**\n   \\[\n   552 \\times 800 = 441600\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(8 \\times 2 = 16\\) (write 6, carry over 1)\n   - \\(8 \\times 5 = 40 + 1 = 41\\) (write 1, carry over 4)\n   - \\(8 \\times 5 = 40 + 4 = 44\\)\n   - Multiply by 100: \\(4416 \\times 100 = 441600\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   2760 + 16560 + 441600\n   \\]\n   - First, add the first two results:\n     \\[\n     2760 + 16560 = 19320\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to the third partial product:\n     \\[\n     19320 + 441600 = 460920\n     \\]\n\n### Answer\nThe product of 552 and 835 is \\boxed{460920}.",
