 Answer**\nThe product of 263 and 361 is \\boxed{94943}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 263 and 361, we break it down into partial products based on the digits of 361 and their place values:\n\n1. **Multiply 263 by the ones place digit (1):**\n   \\[\n   263 \\times 1 = 263\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 263 by the tens place digit (60):**\n   \\[\n   263 \\times 60 = 263 \\times 6 \\times 10 = 1578 \\times 10 = 15780\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 263 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   263 \\times 300 = 263 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 789 \\times 100 = 78900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n263 + 15780 + 78900\n\\]\n\nAdding these step by step:\n\\[\n263 + 15780 = 16043\n\\]\n\\[\n16043 + 78900 = 94943\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{94943}\\).", '']
