e just go through the original reasoning steps again as per the template.\n\nThe problem says:\n\nWhat is the product of 202 and 312?\n\nReasoning:\n\nLet's think step by step. 312 has three digits, so three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 202 by the ones place digit (2) of 312: 202 ×2 = 404.\n\n2. Multiply 202 by the tens place digit (1) of 312. Wait, but the tens place digit is 1, but since it's the tens place, it's actually 10. So, 202 × 10 = 2020.\n\n3. Multiply 202 by the hundreds place digit (3) of 312. Since it's the hundreds place, it's 300. So, 202 × 300 = 60,600.\n\nThen sum all the step results: 404 + 2020 + 60,600 = ?\n\nCalculating:\n\nFirst, 404 + 2020 = 2424.\n\n2424 + 60,600 = 63,024.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 63,024.\n\nSo the answer should be 63,024. All the steps check out. I don't see any errors in the reasoning. Each part is broken down correctly, considering the place values, and the arithmetic adds up. So I'm confident that's the correct answer.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 202 and 312 is \\boxed{63024}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 202 and 312?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 312 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 202 by the ones place digit 2 of 312:  \n   \\(202 \\times 2 = 404\\).\n2. Multiply 202 by the tens place digit 10 of 312:  \n   \\(202 \\times 10 = 2020\\).\n3. Multiply 202 by the hundreds place digit 300 of 312:  \n   \\(202 \\times 300 = 60600\\).\n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(404 + 2020 + 60600 = 63024\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{63024}\\).", '']
