89,600\n\n----------\n\nAdding:\n\nUnits:8+0=8\n\nTens:9+0=9\n\nHundreds:9+6=15 → write 5, carryover1\n\nThousands:4+9=13 plus 1 carried over is 14 → write 4, carryover1\n\nTen-thousands:2+8=10 plus 1 carried over is 11 → write 1, carryover1\n\nHundred-thousands: 6 (from 689,600) plus 1 carried over =7.\n\nSo the result is 714,598. Hmm. But let me confirm with another method to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should check using another multiplication method, like the distributive property.\n\n862 × 829 = 862 × (800 + 20 +9) = 862×800 +862×20 +862×9, which is exactly what I did before. So that's correct.\n\nCalculating each term:\n\n862×800: 862×8=6,896 → ×100 is 689,600.\n\n862×20: 862×2=1,724 → ×10 is 17,240.\n\n862×9: 7,758. So adding those gives 689,600 +17,240 = 706,840; then +7,758 → 706,840 +7,758 = 714,598. Yes, same result.\n\nTherefore, the final product should be 714,598. Wait, but I initially thought 714,598, but let me confirm once more with a calculator approach.\n\nAlternatively, compute 862 ×829:\n\nLet me do 862 × 800 = 689,600\n\n862 ×29 = ?\n\nWait, 862 ×29 = 862×(30-1) = 862×30 -862×1 = 25,860 -862 = 24,998.\n\nTherefore, total is 689,600 +24,998 = 714,598. Yep, same answer.\n\nSo the previous steps are correct. So the answer is 714,598.\n\nWait but in the initial problem statement's example, they had three steps because the second number had three digits, so similarly here, the reasoning should follow the three partial products (hundreds, tens, ones). The user's template example had 153 (three digits) so three steps. Here, 829 is also three digits, so same structure.\n\nSo, the steps would be:\n\n1. Multiply 862 by 9 (ones place) → 7,758.\n\n2. Multiply 862 by 20 (tens place) → 17,240.\n\n3. Multiply 862 by 800 (hundreds place) → 689,600.\n\nThen sum those three: 7,758 +17,240 +689,600 = 714,598.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 714,598.\n\nBut let me just verify once more with another method to be absolutely sure. Let's compute 862 ×829 using another approach, like the standard multiplication vertically:\n\n   862\n\n× 829\n\n--------\n\nFirst, multiply by 9:\n\n862 ×9:\n\n2×9=18, write 8 carryover1.\n\n6×9=54 +1=55, write5 carryover5.\n\n8×9=72 +5=77, write77. So 7,758. Correct.\n\nNext, multiply by 2 (tens place, so actually 20):\n\n862 ×2 (but shifted one position to the left):\n\n2×2=4, write 4.\n\n6×2=12, write 2 carryover1.\n\n8×2=16 +1=17. So 1,724, but shifted one position → 17,240. Correct.\n\nMultiply by 8 (hundreds place, so 800):\n\n862 ×8 (shifted two positions):\n\n2×8=16, write6 carryover1.\n\n6×8=48 +1=49, write9 carryover4.\n\n8×8=64 +4=68. So 6,896, shifted two → 689,600. Correct.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n7,758\n\n17,240\n\n689,600\n\nAdding first two: 7,758 +17,240 =24,998\n\n24,998 +689,600 = 714,598. Yes, that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is 714,598. I think I was just overchecking, but better safe than sorry. So the answer should be 714,598.\n</think>", '']
