vely, use the standard multiplication algorithm:\n\nMultiply 928 by 2 (units):\n\n928 ×2 =1,856\n\nMultiply 928 by 3 (tens place, so shifted left one):\n\n928 ×3 =2,784 → written as 27,840\n\nMultiply 928 by2 (hundreds place, shifted two left):\n\n928 ×2 =1,856 → written as 185,600\n\nAdding them up:\n\n1,856\n\n27,840\n\n185,600\n\nTotal is 215,296. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 215,296.\n\nI think that's solid. I don't see any mistakes in the calculations. All methods converge to the same result. So I'm confident that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 928 and 232 is \\boxed{215296}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 928 and 232, we break down the multiplication step by step based on the place values of the digits in 232.\n\n1. **Multiply 928 by the ones place digit (2):**\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 2 = 1856\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 928 by the tens place digit (30):**\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 30 = 928 \\times 3 \\times 10 = 2784 \\times 10 = 27840\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 928 by the hundreds place digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   928 \\times 200 = 928 \\times 2 \\times 100 = 1856 \\times 100 = 185600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n1856 + 27840 + 185600\n\\]\n\nAdding these step-by-step:\n\\[\n1856 + 27840 = 29696\n\\]\n\\[\n29696 + 185600 = 215296\n\\]\n\nThus, the final product of 928 and 232 is \\(\\boxed{215296}\\).", '']
