      "text": "280,300 plus the remaining 288. Wait, wait a second, no. Wait, 7,288 is 7,000 + 288. So adding 273,300 + 7,000 gives 280,300, then adding the remaining 288 gives 280,300 + 288 = 280,588. Wait, that can't be right because 273,300 + 7,288 is actually 273,300 + 7,288 = 280,588. Hmm, but let me check again. Maybe I made a mistake here.\n\nWait, 273,300 plus 7,288:\n\n273,300  \n+\u00a0 7,288  \n=?\n\nStarting from the right: 0 + 8 =8, 0 +8=8, 3 +2=5, 3 (from 273,300's hundreds place) plus 7 (from 7,288's thousands place) would be 10 in the thousands place. Wait, maybe breaking it down:\n\n273,300 + 7,000 = 280,300\n\nThen add 288: 280,300 + 200 = 280,500; then +88 = 280,588. So total is 280,588.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with another method to be sure. Let me do the multiplication straight up:\n\n911 \u00d7 308.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute it as (900 + 11) \u00d7 (300 + 8) and expand it using distributive property:\n\n= 900\u00d7300 + 900\u00d78 + 11\u00d7300 + 11\u00d78\n\nCompute each term:\n\n900\u00d7300 = 270,000\n\n900\u00d78 = 7,200\n\n11\u00d7300 = 3,300\n\n11\u00d78 = 88\n\nAdding all together: 270,000 + 7,200 = 277,200; then +3,300 = 280,500; then +88 = 280,588. Okay, that matches the previous total. So that's correct.\n\nWait, but in my initial step-by-step breakdown, when I broke down 308 into 300 +0 +8, I had:\n\nOnes place: 911\u00d78 =7,288\n\nTens place: 911\u00d70\u00d710=0\n\nHundreds place: 911\u00d73\u00d7100=273,300\n\nAdding those gives 273,300 + 0 +7,288 = 280,588. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, so then why did I initially think I might have made a mistake? Maybe I confused myself with the addition steps, but both methods give 280,588. So that's the right answer.\n\nBut let me check once more using another approach. Let's do the multiplication vertically:\n\n       911  \n     \u00d7308  \n     -------\n\nFirst, multiply 911 by 8 (the ones place):\n\n911 \u00d7 8:\n\n1\u00d78=8, 1\u00d78=8, 9\u00d78=72. Wait, actually, written out:\n\n    911  \n  \u00d7  8  \n  ------\n   7288 (which matches previous)\n\nThen multiply 911 by the tens place, which is 0. Since it's the tens place, we shift one position to the left, but since the digit is 0, it's 0 shifted over. So that line would be 0000.\n\nThen multiply by the hundreds place, which is 3. But since it's the hundreds place, we shift two positions to the left. So 911 \u00d73 =2733, then shifted two places becomes 273300.\n\nNow add the three lines:\n\n7288  \n+\u00a0 0000 (shifted one)  \n+273300 (shifted two)  \n= 7288 + 273300 = 280,588. Yep, same result.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 280,588.\n\nWait, but let me confirm with a calculator-like approach. Let's do 911 \u00d7 300 = 273,300, and 911 \u00d78=7,288. Adding them gives 273,300 +7,288=280,588. All methods concur. Okay, so the answer is correct.\n\nSo the step-by-step breakdown would be:\n\n1. Multiply 911 by 8 (ones place): 7,288\n\n2. Multiply 911 by 0 (tens place, which is 0\u00d710=0): 0\n\n3. Multiply 911 by 300 (hundreds place): 273,300\n\nSum them all: 7,288 + 0 + 273,300 = 280,588\n\nTherefore, the product is 280,588.\n\nI should make sure that in the reasoning, each step is clearly laid out as per the template. The user mentioned that for number2 such as 153 (three digits), so breaking into three steps. In this case, 308 is three digits, so three steps, even though the middle digit is 0. So the reasoning should include all three steps, even if one of them is zero. That way, the student can see that even if a digit is zero, it's still part of the process.\n\nSo, in the answer section, the sum would be 7,288 + 0 + 273,300, leading to the final answer. Alright, that seems solid. I think that's all. I don't see any mistakes now.\n</think>\n\n",
