distributive property:\n\n907 ×314 = 907 ×(300 +10 +4) = 907×300 +907×10 +907×4, which is exactly what we did. So that's the same as above.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can compute 907 ×314 as follows:\n\nFirst, note that 314 is 300 +14. So 907×300 =272,100 and 907×14. Let's compute 907×14:\n\n907 ×10 =9,070.\n\n907 ×4 =3,628.\n\nAdding those gives 9,070 +3,628 =12,698. Then add that to 272,100 gives the same 284,798.\n\nHmm, so all methods lead to 284,798. Wait, but let me check with a calculator approach, but since I can't use a calculator, perhaps break it down differently.\n\nAlternatively, maybe compute 900×314 and 7×314, then add them together.\n\n900 ×314 = 900×300 +900×14 = 270,000 +12,600 =282,600.\n\nThen 7×314 =2,198.\n\nAdding those: 282,600 +2,198 =284,798. Same result. Okay, so that seems consistent.\n\nTherefore, the final product is 284,798.\n\nWait, but let me check once more, just to be thorough. Let me try another way:.\n\nLet me compute 907 ×314 step by step:\n\nFirst, 907 ×4 =3,628.\n\nThen, 907 ×10 =9,070.\n\nThen, 907 ×300 =272,100.\n\nAdding them all: 3,628 +9,070 is 12,698. Then 12,698 +272,100 is 284,798.\n\nYes, that's the same as before.\n\nHmm. So I think that's the correct answer. Let me just see if there was any miscalculation in the steps.\n\nWait, when I did 907 ×3, I had 900×3=2,700 and 7×3=21, totaling 2,721. That's correct. Then multiplied by 100 gives 272,100. That's right.\n\nAdding the three partial products again: 3,628 (ones place), 9,070 (tens place shifted), 272,100 (hundreds shifted). So adding the first two gives 12,698, then adding to the third gives 284,798. Yes.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I can use another method like the lattice method, but that might be time-consuming, but let me try a small part.\n\nAlternatively, let me see if 907 ×300 is 272,100. Yes. 907 ×10 is 9,070. 907 ×4 is 3,628. All correct. So adding those together, the total must be correct.\n\nTherefore, I think the answer is 284,798.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 907 and 314 is \\boxed{284798}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 907 and 314?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 314 has three digits, so we can break down the multiplication into three steps.\n1. Multiply 907 by the ones place digit (4) of 314:\n   \\[\n   907 \\times 4 = 3628\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 907 by the tens place digit (10) of 314:\n   \\[\n   907 \\times 10 = 9070\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 907 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 314:\n   \\[\n   907 \\times 300 = 272100\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n3628 + 9070 + 272100 = 284798\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{284798}.", '']
