times 9 = 1764\\), then add a zero to account for the tens place: \\(1764 \\times 10 = 17640\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 196 by the hundreds place digit (500):**\n   \\[\n   196 \\times 500 = 98000\n   \\]\n   Calculation: \\(196 \\times 5 = 980\\), then add three zeros to account for the hundreds place: \\(980 \\times 100 = 98000\\).\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n1764 + 17640 + 98000\n\\]\n\n- First, add \\(1764\\) and \\(17640\\):\n  \\[\n  1764 + 17640 = 19404\n  \\]\n\n- Then, add the result to \\(98000\\):\n  \\[\n  19404 + 98000 = 117404\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 196 and 599 is \\(\\boxed{117404}\\).",
