oduct of 209 and 826, we can use the standard multiplication method by breaking down the multiplication into partial products based on the place values of the digits in 826.\n\n1. **Multiply 209 by the ones place digit (6):**\n   \\[\n   209 \\times 6 = 1254\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 209 by the tens place digit (20):**\n   \\[\n   209 \\times 20 = 4180\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 209 by the hundreds place digit (800):**\n   \\[\n   209 \\times 800 = 167200\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1254 + 4180 + 167200\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the ones and tens place multiplications:\n\\[\n1254 + 4180 = 5434\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to the hundreds place multiplication:\n\\[\n5434 + 167200 = 172634\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 209 and 826 is \\(\\boxed{172634}\\).", '']
