:\n   \\[\n   851 \\times 6 = 5106\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 851 by the tens place digit (10) of 816:\n   \\[\n   851 \\times 10 = 8510\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 851 by the hundreds place digit (800) of 816:\n   \\[\n   851 \\times 800 = 680800\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial results:\n\\[\n5106 + 8510 + 680800\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two results:\n\\[\n5106 + 8510 = 13616\n\\]\n\nThen add this result to the third partial product:\n\\[\n13616 + 680800 = 694416\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{694416}\\).", '']
