2):  \n   \\(347 \\times 2 = 694\\).  \n2. Multiply 347 by the tens place digit (60):  \n   \\(347 \\times 60 = 20,\\!820\\).  \n3. Multiply 347 by the hundreds place digit (200):  \n   \\(347 \\times 200 = 69,\\!400\\).  \n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(694 + 20,\\!820 + 69,\\!400 = 90,\\!914\\).  \n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{90914}.", '']
