So that's consistent. Therefore, I think that's the correct answer. I don't see any errors in my calculations now. So the final product should be 235,672.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 662 and 356 is \\boxed{235672}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 662 and 356, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the digits of 356:\n\n1. **Multiply 662 by 6 (ones place):**\n   \\[\n   662 \\times 6 = 3972\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(600 \\times 6 = 3600\\), \\(62 \\times 6 = 372\\), so \\(3600 + 372 = 3972\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 662 by 50 (tens place):**\n   \\[\n   662 \\times 50 = 33100\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(662 \\times 5 = 3310\\), then multiply by 10 to get \\(33100\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 662 by 300 (hundreds place):**\n   \\[\n   662 \\times 300 = 198600\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(662 \\times 3 = 1986\\), then multiply by 100 to get \\(198600\\).\n\nNext, sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n3972 + 33100 + 198600\n\\]\n\n- First, add \\(3972 + 33100\\):\n  \\[\n  3972 + 33100 = 37072\n  \\]\n\n- Then add the result to \\(198600\\):\n  \\[\n  37072 + 198600 = 235672\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 662 and 356 is \\(\\boxed{235672}\\).",
