final_output:  ["476,982. Wait, let me check again to make sure I didn't make an addition error. \n\nWait, 17,082 plus 459,900. Breaking it down: 459,900 + 17,000 = 476,900, then add the remaining 82 to get 476,982. That seems right. \n\nBut let me verify using another method to be safe. Maybe the standard algorithm:\n\nMultiplying 657 × 726:\n\nFirst line: 657 × 6 = 3,942\n\nSecond line: 657 × 20 = 13,140 (shifted one position to the left)\n\nThird line: 657 × 700 = 459,900 (shifted two positions left)\n\nAdding them:\n\n3,942  \n13,140  \n+459,900  \n= ?\n\nAdding first two: 3,942 +13,140 = 17,082. Then 17,082 +459,900 = 476,982. Okay, that matches.\n\nAlternatively, maybe cross-check using another multiplication method, like breaking down the numbers:\n\n657 × 726 = 657 × (700 + 20 +6) = 657×700 +657×20 +657×6, which is exactly what we did. So that's correct.\n\nHmm, seems like the answer is 476,982. I think that's right. Let me just confirm once more with a calculator-style approach:\n\n657 × 700 = 459,900\n\n657 × 20 = 13,140\n\n657 ×6 = 3,942\n\nAdding those three: 459,900 +13,140 = 473,040. Then +3,942 gives 476,982. Yes, same result. Okay, confident now. The final product is 476,982.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 657 and 726 is \\boxed{476982}.\n</think>", '']
