      "text": "102,372. Wait, but let me check that again. 11,172 + 91,200:.\n\nAdding 11,172 and 91,200:\n\n91,200 + 10,000 = 101,200.\n\n101,200 + 1,172 = 102,372. Yes, that's right.\n\nHmm, let me cross-verify using another method to be sure. Maybe using the standard multiplication algorithm.\n\nMultiplying 228 by 449:\n\nFirst, write it as:\n\n\u2003\u2003228\n\u00d7449\n--------\n\nStart with multiplying by the ones digit (9):\n\n228 \u00d7 9:.\n\n8\u00d79=72, write down 2 and carryover 7.\n\n2\u00d79=18 +7=25, write 5 and carryover 2.\n\n2\u00d79=18 +2=20. So that gives 2052.\n\nThen multiply by the tens digit (4), but shifted one position to the left (since it's the tens place):\n\n228 \u00d74:\n\n8\u00d74=32, write 2, carryover 3.\n\n2\u00d74=8 +3=11, write 1, carryover 1.\n\n2\u00d74=8 +1=9. So 912, but shifted one place becomes 9120.\n\nThen multiply by the hundreds digit (4), shifted two places:\n\n228 \u00d74 again, but shifted two places: 228\u00d74=912, so with two zeros becomes 91,200.\n\nAdding all three: 2052 +9120=11,172; 11,172 +91,200=102,372. Same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe use the distributive property another way: (200 +28) \u00d7 (400 +40 +9). But that might be more complicated, but just to check.\n\nAlternatively, compute 228\u00d7449:\n\nLet me think of 449 as 450 -1. Then:\n\n228 \u00d7 (450 -1) = 228\u00d7450 - 228\u00d71.\n\n228\u00d7450 = 228\u00d745\u00d710.\n\nCompute 228\u00d745 first:.\n\n228\u00d740 =9120, 228\u00d75=1140. So 9120+1140=10260. Then \u00d710 is 102,600.\n\nSubtract 228: 102,600 -228=102,372. Yep, same answer. Okay, so that confirms it.\n\nTherefore, the product is 102,372.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 228 and 449 is \\boxed{102372}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 228 and 449, we break down 449 into its hundreds, tens, and ones places: 400, 40, and 9. We then multiply 228 by each part individually and sum the results.\n\n1. **Multiply 228 by the ones place digit 9:**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 9 = 2052\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(200 \\times 9 = 1800\\) and \\(28 \\times 9 = 252\\), so \\(1800 + 252 = 2052\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 228 by the tens place digit 40:**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 40 = 9120\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(228 \\times 4 = 912\\), then add a zero to account for the tens place: \\(912 \\times 10 = 9120\\).\n\n3. **Multiply 228 by the hundreds place digit 400:**\n   \\[\n   228 \\times 400 = 91200\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(228 \\times 4 = 912\\), then add two zeros to account for the hundreds place: \\(912 \\times 100 = 91200\\).\n\nNext, we sum the results of the three multiplications:\n\\[\n2052 + 9120 + 91200\n\\]\n\n- Adding \\(2052\\) and \\(9120\\):\n  \\[\n  2052 + 9120 = 11172\n  \\]\n\n- Adding the result to \\(91200\\):\n  \\[\n  11172 + 91200 = 102372\n  \\]\n\nThus, the product of 228 and 449 is \\(\\boxed{102372}\\).",
