 partial product: 54,720.\n\nThird partial product: 273,600.\n\nAdding them up step by step. Let's start with 4,104 +54,720. Let's add those:.\n\n4,104.\n\n+54,720.\n\n= 58,824 (because 4,000 +54,000 =58,000; 104 +720=824. Total 58,824).\n\nThen add 273,600 to that:.\n\n58,824 +273,600</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
