rst multiply 402 by 3: 1206  \nThen 402 x40: 16,080 (shift one position to the left)  \nThen 402 x800: 321,600 (shift two positions to the left)  \nAdding all three gives the total. \n\nSo the final answer should be 338,886. I think that's correct. Let me check with a calculator in my mind. \n\nAlternatively, 400*800 = 320,000. Then 400*43 = 400*(40+3)= 16,000 +1,200 =17,200. Then 2*843 =1,686. So total would be 320,000 +17,200 = 337,200 +1,686 =338,886. Yes, same answer. So that's correct.\n\nI think that's solid. So the steps are as above.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 402 and 843?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 843 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps:\n1. Multiply 402 by the ones place digit (3):  \n   \\(402 \\times 3 = 1,\\!206\\).\n2. Multiply 402 by the tens place digit (40):  \n   \\(402 \\times 40 = 16,\\!080\\).\n3. Multiply 402 by the hundreds place digit (800):  \n   \\(402 \\times 800 = 321,\\!600\\).  \nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(1,\\!206 + 16,\\!080 + 321,\\!600 = 338,\\!886\\).  \nAnswer:  \nThe final computed product is \\boxed{338886}.",
