,860. Let's see: 3000 + 15,000 is 18,000. Then 172 + 860 is 1,032. So adding those gives 18,000 + 1,032 = 19,032. Wait, no, that can't be right. Wait, maybe I should add them directly. 3172 + 15,860. Let's do 3172 + 15,860. .\n\nStarting from the right: 2 + 0 = 2. 7 + 6 = 13, carry over 1. 1 + 8 + 5 = 14, plus the carried 1 is 15. Carry over 1 again. 3 + 5 = 8 plus the carried 1 is 9. Then the 1 from the 15,860. Wait, maybe I messed up the place values. Let me write it out:.\n\n  3172.\n+15860.\n--------.\nAdding the units: 2 + 0 = 2.\nTens: 7 + 6 = 13, write 3, carry 1.\nHundreds: 1 + 8 = 9, plus the 1 carried is 10, so write 0 and carry 1.\nThousands: 3 + 5 = 8, plus the 1 carried is 9.\nTen-thousands: 1 from the 15,860. So total is 19,032? Wait, but 3172 + 15,860. Let me do it another way. 15,860 + 3,000 is 18,860, then add 172: 18,860 + 172 = 19,032. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add that to 237,900. So 19,032 + 237,900. Let's see, 19,032 + 200,000 is 219,032. Then add 37,900: 219,032 + 37,900</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
