o 240,000 - 2268 = 237,732? Wait, no, that might not be the right way. Alternatively, maybe approximate both numbers: 793 is ~800, 324 is ~300. 800*300 = 240,000. The actual numbers are a bit less and a bit more. 793 is 7 less than 800, so 7*324=2268 less. But 324 is 24 more than 300, so 800*24 = 19,200 more. So net difference: 19,200 - 2,268 = 16,932. So total would be 240,000 +16,932=256,932. Which matches the previous result. That approximation method gives the same answer, so that's reassuring.\n\nTherefore, I think the final answer is correct: 256,932.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 793 and 324 is \\boxed{256932}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 793 and 324, we can break down the multiplication using the standard method:\n\n1. **Multiply 793 by the ones place digit (4) of 324:**\n   \\[\n   793 \\times 4 = 3172\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(700 \\times 4 = 2800\\), \\(90 \\times 4 = 360\\), \\(3 \\times 4 = 12\\)\n   - Sum: \\(2800 + 360 + 12 = 3172\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 793 by the tens place digit (20) of 324:**\n   \\[\n   793 \\times 20 = 15860\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(793 \\times 2 = 1586\\), then add a zero: \\(1586 \\times 10 = 15860\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 793 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 324:**\n   \\[\n   793 \\times 300 = 237900\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(793 \\times 3 = 2379\\), then add two zeros: \\(2379 \\times 100 = 237900\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   3172 + 15860 + 237900\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(3172 + 15860\\):\n     \\[\n     3172 + 15860 = 19032\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(237900\\):\n     \\[\n     19032 + 237900 = 256932\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 793 and 324 is \\(\\boxed{256932}\\).",
