 match digits:\n\n 01578\n\n+55230\n\n=?\n\nAdding each column:\n\nUnits: 8 +0=8\n\nTens:7 +3=10, write 0 carryover 1\n\nHundreds:5 +2=7 plus 1 is 8\n\nThousands:1 +5=6\n\nTen-thousands: 0 +5=5\n\nWait, so the total would be 56808. Yes, that's correct. Then adding 78900:\n\n56808 +78900.\n\nLet me write them aligned:\n\n 56808\n\n+78900\n\n--------\n\nAdding units:8+0=8\n\nTens:0+0=0\n\nHundreds:8 +9=17, write 7 carryover 1\n\nThousands:6 +8=14 plus 1=15, write 5 carryover 1\n\nTen-thousands:5 +7=12 plus 1=13\n\nSo total is 135,708. Correct. So I think that's accurate.\n\nTherefore, the answer should be 135,708.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 789 and 172 is \\boxed{135708}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 789 and 172, we break it down using the standard multiplication method:\n\n1. **Multiply 789 by the ones place digit (2) of 172:**\n   \\[\n   789 \\times 2 = 1578\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 789 by the tens place digit (70) of 172:**\n   \\[\n   789 \\times 70 = 789 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 5523 \\times 10 = 55230\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 789 by the hundreds place digit (100) of 172:**\n   \\[\n   789 \\times 100 = 78900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1578 + 55230 + 78900\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(1578\\) and \\(55230\\):\n\\[\n1578 + 55230 = 56808\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to \\(78900\\):\n\\[\n56808 + 78900 = 135708\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{135708}\\).", '']
