0×300=60,000. Our result is 64,749 which is in that range. So that seems plausible.\n\nAlternatively, 200×340 = 68,000. Subtract (9×340) = 3,060 gives 64,940. Hmm, but since it's actually 191×339, which is 200-9 times 340-1, so maybe not the best estimation, but 64k seems reasonable.\n\nTherefore, I think the correct product is 64,749.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 191 and 339 is \\boxed{64749}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 191 and 339, we can use the standard multiplication algorithm by breaking it down into partial products and then summing them up.\n\n1. **Multiply 191 by the ones place digit (9) of 339:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 9 = 1719\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 191 by the tens place digit (30) of 339:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 30 = 5730\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 191 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 339:**\n   \\[\n   191 \\times 300 = 57300\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1719 + 5730 + 57300\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two partial products:\n\\[\n1719 + 5730 = 7449\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to the third partial product:\n\\[\n7449 + 57300 = 64749\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 191 and 339 is \\(\\boxed{64749}\\).", '']
