 of 5,580 +65,100=70,680; 70,680 +558,000 = 628,680.\n\nTherefore, the product is 628,680. I think that's correct. Let me just check with a calculator-like approach. Since 930 is 93*10, and 676 is 676. So 93*676 = ?\n\nCalculating 93 ×676:\n\nFirst, 90×676 = 60,840. Then 3×676=2,028. Adding those gives 60,840 +2,028 =62,868. Then multiply by 10 (since 930 is 93×10), so 628,680. Yep, same answer. So that's correct. I think that's solid. So the final answer should be 628,680.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 930 and 676 is \\boxed{628680}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 930 and 676, we break down 676 into its place values (600, 70, and 6) and multiply each part by 930, then sum the results.\n\n1. Multiply 930 by 600:\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 600 = 930 \\times 6 \\times 100 = 5580 \\times 100 = 558000\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 930 by 70:\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 70 = 930 \\times 7 \\times 10 = 6510 \\times 10 = 65100\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 930 by 6:\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 6 = 5580\n   \\]\n\nSumming all the results:\n\\[\n558000 + 65100 + 5580 = 628680\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 930 and 676 is \\(\\boxed{628680}\\).", '']
