83×9)×100. 283×9 is 2,547 → 254,700.\n\n283×6 =1,698.\n\nSo subtracting: 254,700 -1,698 =253,002. Same result. Okay, that's a good check.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using the distributive property another way. Let me see.\n\nAlternatively, 894 can be written as 800+90+4, so 283×800 +283×90 +283×4, which is exactly the same as the initial method. So that's consistent.\n\nTherefore, the product is 253,002. I think that's correct.\n\nWait, but just to ensure, maybe do the multiplication step by step again:\n\n283 × 894:\n\nStart with 4×283:\n\n4×3=12, write down 2, carryover 1.\n\n4×8=32 +1=33, write 3, carryover 3.\n\n4×2=8 +3=11. So that's 1,132. Correct.\n\nThen 9 (tens place):\n\n9×3=27, write 7, carryover 2.\n\n9×8=72 +2=74, write 4, carryover7.\n\n9×2=18 +7=25. So that gives 2,547. But since it's the tens place, shift one to the left: 25,470. Correct.\n\nThen 8 (hundreds place):\n\n8×3=24, write 4, carryover2.\n\n8×8=64 +2=66, write 6, carryover6.\n\n8×2=16 +6=22. So that gives 2,264. Shifting two places: 226,400. Correct.\n\nAdding all three:\n\n1,132\n\n25,470 → total so far 26,602\n\n226,400 → total 253,002. Yes.\n\nTherefore, the final answer should be 253,002.\n\nI think that's solid. Let me just confirm with a calculator-style multiplication:\n\n283 ×894.\n\nLet me compute 283 × 800 =226,400\n\n283 ×90=25,470\n\n283×4=1,132. Adding those gives 226,400 +25,470 is 251,870, plus 1,132 is 253,002. Yep. So that's correct.\n\nAlright, confident now.\n\n</think>", '']
