 digits of the second number (384):\n\n1. **Multiply 402 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 4 = 1608\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 402 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 80 = 402 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 3216 \\times 10 = 32160\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 402 by the hundreds place digit (300):**\n   \\[\n   402 \\times 300 = 402 \\times 3 \\times 100 = 1206 \\times 100 = 120600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n1608 + 32160 + 120600\n\\]\n\nAdding step-by-step:\n\\[\n1608 + 32160 = 33768\n\\]\n\\[\n33768 + 120600 = 154368\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{154368}\\).", '']
