67*10=7,670 and 767*2=1,534. So total is 7,670+1,534=9,204.\n\nSo 383,500 -9,204 = ?\n\n383,500 - 9,000 = 374,500. Then subtract 204 more: 374,500 -204 = 374,296. Same answer. So that checks out.\n\nTherefore, the product is indeed 374,296. I think that's correct.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 767 and 488 is \\boxed{374296}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 767 and 488, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 488:\n\n1. **Multiply 767 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   767 \\times 8 = 6136\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(700 \\times 8 = 5600\\)\n   - \\(60 \\times 8 = 480\\)\n   - \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\)\n   - Sum: \\(5600 + 480 + 56 = 6136\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 767 by the tens place digit (80):**\n   \\[\n   767 \\times 80 = 61360\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - First calculate \\(767 \\times 8 = 6136\\)\n   - Then multiply by 10: \\(6136 \\times 10 = 61360\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 767 by the hundreds place digit (400):**\n   \\[\n   767 \\times 400 = 306800\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - First calculate \\(767 \\times 4 = 3068\\)\n   - Then multiply by 100: \\(3068 \\times 100 = 306800\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   6136 + 61360 + 306800 = 374296\n   \\]\n   Calculation steps:\n   - \\(6136 + 61360 = 67496\\)\n   - \\(67496 + 306800 = 374296\\)\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{374296}\\).",
