ight be more complicated. Alternatively, check with calculator steps?\n\nAlternatively, compute 253 \u00d7244.\n\nAlternatively, 253 \u00d7244 =253\u00d7(200+44)=253\u00d7200 +253\u00d744.\n\n253\u00d7200 is 50,600 as before.\n\n253\u00d744: Let's compute that. 253\u00d740=10,120 and 253\u00d74=1,012. Adding those gives 10,120+1,012=11,132. Then 50,600 +11,132=61,732. Yep, same result.\n\nAlternatively, maybe do 253\u00d7244 as (250 +3)(240 +4). Let's see:\n\n(250+3)(240+4) =250\u00d7240 +250\u00d74 +3\u00d7240 +3\u00d74.\n\n250\u00d7240 =60,000 (since 25\u00d724=600, so times 100).\n\n250\u00d74=1,000.\n\n3\u00d7240=720.\n\n3\u00d74=12.\n\nAdding those together:60,000 +1,000=61,000; 61,000 +720=61,720; 61,720 +12=61,732. Same answer. So that confirms it.\n\nHmm, so I think the answer is 61,732. Let me just check once more with another approach.\n\nAlternatively, using the standard multiplication steps:\n\n\u2003\u2003253\n\n\u00d7244\n\n------------\n\nFirst line: 253 \u00d74 =1,012\n\nSecond line: 253 \u00d74 (tens place, so shifted left one) \u2192 253\u00d740=10,120\n\nThird line:253\u00d72 (hundreds place, shifted left two) \u2192253\u00d7200=50,600\n\nAdding them:\n\n1,012\n\n10,120\n\n50,600\n\nTotal:\n\n1,012 +10,120 =11,132\n\n11,132 +50,600=61,732.\n\nYep, consistent. So I think that's the correct product. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. All different methods give the same result, so I'm confident it's 61,732.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 253 and 244 is \\boxed{61732}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 253 and 244, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 244 (200, 40, and 4):\n\n1. **Multiply 253 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 4 = 1012\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 253 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 40 = 10120\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 253 by the hundreds place digit (200):**\n   \\[\n   253 \\times 200 = 50600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three steps:\n\\[\n1012 + 10120 + 50600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add \\(1012\\) and \\(10120\\):\n\\[\n1012 + 10120 = 11132\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to \\(50600\\):\n\\[\n11132 + 50600 = 61732\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 253 and 244 is \\(\\boxed{61732}\\).",
