4, we break it down into three steps corresponding to each digit's place in 794 (ones, tens, hundreds):\n\n1. **Multiply 103 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   103 \\times 4 = 412\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 103 by the tens place digit (90):**\n   \\[\n   103 \\times 90 = 9270\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 103 by the hundreds place digit (700):**\n   \\[\n   103 \\times 700 = 72100\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three multiplications:\n\\[\n412 + 9270 + 72100\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 412 and 9270:\n\\[\n412 + 9270 = 9682\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to 72100:\n\\[\n9682 + 72100 = 81782\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product of 103 and 794 is \\(\\boxed{81782}\\).", '']
