s. So the third part is 460,200.\n\nNow, I have to add all three results together: 6,136 + 61,360 + 460,200. Let's start adding the first two. 6,136 + 61,360. Adding the thousands: 6,000 + 61,000 is 67,000. Then the hundreds: 136 + 360 is 496. Wait, no, maybe better to do straight addition. 6,136 + 61,360. Let's line them up:.\n\n  6,136.\n+61,360.\n--------.\n 67,496.\n\nYes, that's correct. Now add that to 460,200. So 67,496 + 460,200. Adding the ten thousands: 400,000 + 60,000 = 460,000</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
