 minus 12,600 is 483,400; minus 420 is 482,980. Exactly the same as before. Wow, that worked out. So that confirms it again. \n\nTherefore, I'm confident that the product of 779 and 620 is 482,980. \n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 779 and 620 is \\boxed{482980}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 779 and 620?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 620 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 779 by the ones place digit 0 of 620:\n   \\[\n   779 \\times 0 = 0\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 779 by the tens place digit 20 of 620:\n   \\[\n   779 \\times 20 = 15580\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 779 by the hundreds place digit 600 of 620:\n   \\[\n   779 \\times 600 = 467400\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n0 + 15580 + 467400 = 482980\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{482980}.",
