\n   Since this is the ones place, the result is \\(0\\).\n\n2. **Multiply 930 by the tens place digit (1) and shift one position to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 10):**\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 10 = 9300\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 930 by the hundreds place digit (2) and shift two positions to the left (equivalent to multiplying by 200):**\n   \\[\n   930 \\times 200 = 186000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n0 + 9300 + 186000 = 195300\n\\]\n\nWe can verify this result using another method by first removing the zeros from 930 and 210, multiplying the remaining numbers, and then adding the zeros back:\n- Remove one zero from each number: \\(930 \\rightarrow 93\\) and \\(210 \\rightarrow 21\\)\n- Multiply the remaining numbers: \\(93 \\times 21 = 1953\\)\n- Add the two zeros back: \\(1953 \\times 100 = 195300\\)\n\nBoth methods confirm that the product of 930 and 210 is \\(\\boxed{195300}\\).",
