iplying 464 \u00d7365 directly.\n\nLet me write it out vertically:\n\n      464\n\n    \u00d7365\n\n    --------\n\nFirst, multiply 464 by 5 (units place):\n\n464 \u00d75 =2320.\n\nThen multiply 464 by 60 (tens place, so shifted one position left):\n\n464 \u00d76 =2784, so 27840.\n\nThen multiply 464 by 300 (hundreds place, shifted two positions left):\n\n464 \u00d73 =1392, so 139200.\n\nNow adding them up:\n\n2320\n\n27840\n\n+139200\n\n________\n\nLet me add 2320 +27840 first:\n\n2320 +27840:\n\n2000 +27000 =29000; 320 +840 =1160. 29000 +1160 =30160.\n\nThen 30160 +139200:\n\n30160 +139200. Let's see:\n\n30,160 +139,200. 30k +139k =169k. 160 + 200 = 360. So total 169,360. So that's correct.\n\nTherefore, the final answer is 169,360. Wait, but let me confirm with another method just to be sure.\n\nAlternatively, maybe using distributive property:\n\n464 \u00d7365 =464 \u00d7(300 +60 +5) =464\u00d7300 +464\u00d760 +464\u00d75. Which is exactly what I did. So the sum is indeed 139,200 +27,840 +2,320 = 139,200 + 30,160 = 169,360.\n\nHmm. Wait, but the user's initial example had 27\u00d7153. Let me check if that example was correct.\n\nIn the user's first example, they had 27\u00d7153. Let me see what that would be. 27\u00d73=81, 27\u00d750=1350, 27\u00d7100=2700. Sum: 81+1350=1431, +2700=4131. Let me compute 27\u00d7153 directly: 153\u00d727. 153\u00d720=3060, 153\u00d77=1071, total 3060+1071=4131. So that works. So the method is correct.\n\nTherefore, applying the same method to 464\u00d7365 gives 169,360. But wait, let me check with a calculator to be absolutely sure. Since this is a critical step.\n\nWait, since I can't use an actual calculator, let me compute 464 \u00d7365 another way.\n\nLet me compute 464 \u00d7365:\n\nFirst, note that 365 = 350 +15.\n\nSo 464 \u00d7350 =464 \u00d735 \u00d710. Compute 464 \u00d735 first.\n\n464 \u00d735: 464 \u00d730 =13,920; 464 \u00d75=2,320. Adding those gives 13,920 +2,320 =16,240. Then \u00d710 gives 162,400.\n\nThen 464 \u