ply 845 by the hundreds place digit (600):**\n   \\[\n   845 \\times 600 = 507000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these three multiplications:\n\\[\n2535 + 16900 + 507000\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the results of the first two steps:\n\\[\n2535 + 16900 = 19435\n\\]\n\nThen, add this result to the result of the third step:\n\\[\n19435 + 507000 = 526435\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 845 and 623 is \\(\\boxed{526435}\\).",
