:\n\n       988\n     × 804\n     --------\n        3952  (988 × 4)\n       0000   (988 × 0, shifted one position)\n     790400  (988 × 8, shifted two positions)\n     --------\n     794352\n\nAdding those three lines: 3952 + 0 + 790400 = 794,352. Yep, that's the same. So I think that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 988 and 804 is 794,352.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 988 and 804 is \\boxed{794352}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 988 and 804, we can break down the multiplication into steps corresponding to each digit's place value in 804:\n\n1. **Multiply 988 by the ones place digit (4):**\n   \\[\n   988 \\times 4 = 3952\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 988 by the tens place digit (0):**\n   \\[\n   988 \\times 0 = 0 \\quad \\text{(shifted one position to the left)}\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 988 by the hundreds place digit (800):**\n   \\[\n   988 \\times 800 = 988 \\times 8 \\times 100 = 7904 \\times 100 = 790400\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n3952 + 0 + 790400 = 794352\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 988 and 804 is \\(\\boxed{794352}\\).", '']
