, 992 × 5. Let me do that step by step. 900 × 5 is 4500, 90 ×5 is 450, and 2×5 is 10. Adding those together: 4500 + 450 = 4950, plus 10 is 4960. So 992 ×5 is 4960. Then multiply by 100, so that becomes 4960 ×100 = 496000. .\n\nNow I need to add all three results together: 992 (from ones) + 9920 (from tens) + 496000 (from hundreds). Let me add them step by step. .\n\nFirst, add 992 and 9920. 992 + 9920. Let's see, 992 + 9920. 992 + 9000 is 9992, plus 920 more? Wait no, maybe better to line them up:.\n\n   992.\n+ 9920.\n--------.\nLet's align the digits:.\n\n   992.\n+9920.\n= 10912? Wait, 992 + 9920. Let me compute this correctly. 992 plus 9920. 992 + 9000 is 9992, plus 920? Wait, no. Maybe better to think 9920 is 9 thousands, 9 hundreds, 2 tens, 0 ones. Wait no, 9920 is 9 thousands, 9 hundreds, 2 tens. Wait, actually 9920 is 9 (thousands), 9 (hundreds), 2 (tens), 0 (ones). So adding to 992 (which is 0 thousands, 9 hundreds, 9 tens, 2 ones). .\n\nAdding the ones place: 0 + 2 =2. Tens place: 2 + 9 = 11, so write down 1 and carry over 1. Hundreds place: 9 + 9 + 1 (carry) = 19, so write 9 and carry 1. Thousands place: 9 + 0 +1 =10. So total is 10912. Wait, that can't be right. Wait, 992 + 9920. Let me do it numerically: 9920 + 992. 9920 + 900 = 10820, then +92 is 10912. Yes, that's correct.\n\nNow add that to the third part, which is 496,000. So 10,912 + 496,000</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
