r:.\n\n3164 (from the ones).\n+40,680 (from the tens).\n+135,600 (from the hundreds).\n-------------------.\nLet me add them step by step. First, 3164 + 40,680. Let's see, 3000 + 40,000 is 43,000. 164 + 680 = 844. So total is 43,844?.\n\nWait, maybe better to add directly:.\n\n3164.\n+40680.\n= 3164 + 40,680. Adding the thousands: 40,000 + 3,000 = 43,000. Then 680 + 164 = 844. So total 43,844. Then adding the last term: 43,844 + 135,600. .\n\nAdding those together: 43,844 + 135,600. Let's see, 43,844 + 100,000 = 143,844</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
