ltiply 452 by 300 (hundreds place digit is 3, so 3\u00d7100=300).\n\nThen sum all three results: 3164 +40,680 +135,600 = 179,444.\n\nYes, so that's exactly what I did. So the answer is correct. Therefore, I can present the solution accordingly.\n\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 452 and 397?  \n# Reasoning:  \nLet's think step by step. 397 has three digits, so we can break the multiplication into three steps.  \n1. **Multiply 452 by the ones place digit (7):**  \n   \\(452 \\times 7 = 3,\\!164\\).  \n2. **Multiply 452 by the tens place digit (90):**  \n   \\(452 \\times 90 = 40,\\!680\\).  \n3. **Multiply 452 by the hundreds place digit (300):**  \n   \\(452 \\times 300 = 135,\\!600\\).  \n\n**Sum all the step results:**  \n\\[\n3,\\!164 + 40,\\!680 + 135,\\!600 = 179,\\!444\n\\]  \n\nAnswer:  \nNow, sum all the step results: \\(3,\\!164 + 40,\\!680 + 135,\\!600 = 179,\\!444\\).  \nSo, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{179444}\\).",
