messages:  [["Please act as a math teacher and solve the product problem in the given template.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of <<number1 such as 27>> and <<number2 such as 153>>?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. <<number2 153 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.>>\n1. <<Multiply number1 27 by the ones place digit 3 of number2 153>>\n2. <<Multiply number1 27 by the tens place digit 50 of number2 153>>\n<<other digits of number2 if it has>>\nAnswer:\nNow, sum all the step results: <<sum of the results>>.\nSo, the final computed product is <<answer>>.\n####\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 329 and 679?\n# Reasoning:", "<think>\nOkay, let's tackle the problem of multiplying 329 by 679. Hmm, both numbers are three-digit, so this might take a bit of time, but I can break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, I remember that when multiplying large numbers, you can break them down into their place values. So 679 can be split into 600 + 70 + 9. That way, I can multiply each part separately by 329 and then add the results together. Let me write that down:.\n\n329 × 600 = ?.\n329 × 70 = ?.\n329 × 9 = ?.\n\nStarting with the first one: 329 multiplied by 600. Since 600 is 6 times 100, maybe I can do 329 × 6 first and then add two zeros. Let's see, 329 × 6. 300×6 is 1800, and 29×6 is 174, so adding those gives 1800 + 174 = 1974. Then adding two zeros makes it 197,400. Okay, that seems right.\n\nNext, 329 × 70. Similarly, 70 is 7 × 10, so maybe multiply 329 by 7 first. 300×7 is 2100, 20×7 is 140, and 9×7 is 63. Adding those: 2100 + 140 = 2240, plus 63 is 2303. Then multiply by 10 to get 23,030. Wait, hold on, actually, maybe I should have done 329 ×7 first and then add a zero. Let me check that again. 329 ×7: 300×7=2100, 20×7=140, 9×7=63. Adding those gives 2100+140 is 2240, plus 63 is 2303. Then multiplying by 10 gives 23,030. Yeah, that's correct.\n\nNow the last part: 329 ×9. Let's compute that. 300×9=2700, 20×9=180, 9×9=81. Adding those together: 2700 + 180 = 2880, plus 81 gives 2961. So that's 2,961.\n\nNow I need to add all three results together: 197,400 + 23,030 + 2,961. Let me add the first two first. 197,400 + 23,030. Adding the thousands: 197,400 + 20,000 = 217,400. Then adding 3,030 more gives 217,400 + 3,030 = 220,430. Now add the last term: 220,430 + 2,961. Let's see, 220,430 + 2,000 = 222,430</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
