 then add a zero: \\(2485 \\times 10 = 24850\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 355 by the hundreds place digit (300) of 375:**\n   \\[\n   355 \\times 300 = 106500\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(355 \\times 3 = 1065\\), then add two zeros: \\(1065 \\times 100 = 106500\\)\n\n**Sum all the partial products:**\n\\[\n1775 + 24850 + 106500\n\\]\n- First, add \\(1775\\) and \\(24850\\):\n  \\[\n  1775 + 24850 = 26625\n  \\]\n- Then add the result to \\(106500\\):\n  \\[\n  26625 + 106500 = 133125\n  \\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{133125}\\).", '']
