  \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(900 \\times 8 = 7200\\), \\(40 \\times 8 = 320\\), \\(7 \\times 8 = 56\\)\n   - Sum: \\(7200 + 320 + 56 = 7576\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 947 by the tens place digit (80) of 988:**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 80 = 75760\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(947 \\times 8 \\times 10 = 7576 \\times 10 = 75760\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 947 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 988:**\n   \\[\n   947 \\times 900 = 852300\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(947 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 8523 \\times 100 = 852300\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the partial products:**\n   \\[\n   7576 + 75760 + 852300\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(7576\\) and \\(75760\\):\n     \\[\n     7576 + 75760 = 83336\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(852300\\):\n     \\[\n     83336 + 852300 = 935636\n     \\]\n\nThus, the product of 947 and 988 is \\(\\boxed{935636}\\).",
