Answer**\nThe product of 229 and 311 is \\boxed{71219}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 229 and 311?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 311 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 229 by the ones place digit 1 of 311: \\(229 \\times 1 = 229\\).\n2. Multiply 229 by the tens place digit 10 of 311: \\(229 \\times 10 = 2290\\).\n3. Multiply 229 by the hundreds place digit 300 of 311: \\(229 \\times 300 = 68700\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results: \\(229 + 2290 + 68700\\).\n\nCalculating the sum:\n- First, \\(229 + 2290 = 2519\\).\n- Then, \\(2519 + 68700 = 71219\\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\(71219\\).\n\n### Answer:\nThe product of 229 and 311 is \\boxed{71219}.",
