ing by the tens place, each step should be shifted one position to the left, right? So actually, multiplying by the tens digit (3) would be 356 × 3, but then multiplied by 10, hence the zero. So that part is correct. .\n\nNow the hundreds place: 500. So 356 × 500. Let me compute that. 356 × 5 is 1,780, and then adding two zeros gives 178,000. .\n\nSo now I have three components: 2,136 (from the ones), 10,680 (from the tens), and 178,000 (from the hundreds). Now I need to add them all together. Let me line them up properly.\n\nStarting with the largest, 178,000. Adding 10,680: 178,000 + 10,680 = 188,680. Then add 2,136 to that. .\n\n188,680 + 2,136. Let's see: 188,680 + 2,000 is 190,680</think>\nTherefore, the answer is "]]
