 425,584. Yep, that's correct.\n\nSo, I think the final answer is correct. I don't see any mistakes in the steps. So the product of 794 and 536 is 425,584.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 794 and 536 is \\boxed{425584}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 794 and 536, we break it down into partial products based on the place values of the digits in 536:\n\n1. Multiply 794 by the ones place digit (6):\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 6 = 4764\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 794 by the tens place digit (30):\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 30 = 23820\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 794 by the hundreds place digit (500):\n   \\[\n   794 \\times 500 = 397000\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\\[\n4764 + 23820 + 397000\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the first two results:\n\\[\n4764 + 23820 = 28584\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to the third partial product:\n\\[\n28584 + 397000 = 425584\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 794 and 536 is \\(\\boxed{425584}\\).",
