*\nThe product of 491 and 921 is \\boxed{452211}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 491 and 921, we break down the multiplication into steps based on the place values of 921 (hundreds, tens, and ones):\n\n1. **Multiply 491 by the ones place digit (1) of 921:**\n   \\[\n   491 \\times 1 = 491\n   \\]\n\n2. **Multiply 491 by the tens place digit (20) of 921:**\n   \\[\n   491 \\times 20 = 9820\n   \\]\n\n3. **Multiply 491 by the hundreds place digit (900) of 921:**\n   \\[\n   491 \\times 900 = 441900\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum all the partial products:\n\n\\[\n491 + 9820 + 441900\n\\]\n\nFirst, add the smaller partial products:\n\\[\n491 + 9820 = 10311\n\\]\n\nThen add the result to the largest partial product:\n\\[\n10311 + 441900 = 452211\n\\]\n\nThus, the product of 491 and 921 is \\(\\boxed{452211}\\).", '']
