t that might not help much. Alternatively, check using another multiplication method like the lattice method, but that might take longer. Alternatively, see if 469,908 divided by 513 equals 916.\n\nLet me do a quick division check: 469,908 \u00f7513.\n\nFirst, approximate: 513 \u00d7900 = 461,700.\n\nSubtract that from 469,908: 469,908 -461,700 =8,208.\n\nNow, 513 \u00d716 = 8,208. So total is 900+16=916. Perfect. So that confirms that 513 \u00d7916=469,908.\n\nSo, after verifying through multiple methods and cross-checking, I believe the product is 469,908.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 916 and 513 is \\boxed{469908}.\n</think>\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 916 and 513?\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 513 has three digits, so we can reason in three steps.\n1. Multiply 916 by the ones place digit 3 of 513:  \n   \\(916 \\times 3 = 2748\\).\n2. Multiply 916 by the tens place digit 10 of 513:  \n   \\(916 \\times 10 = 9160\\).\n3. Multiply 916 by the hundreds place digit 500 of 513:  \n   \\(916 \\times 500 = 458000\\).\n\nNow, sum all the step results:  \n\\(2748 + 9160 + 458000 = 469908\\).\n\nSo, the final computed product is \\boxed{469908}.",
