s it. So I'm confident the product is 351,909.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 641 and 549 is \\boxed{351909}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 641 and 549, we break down the multiplication step by step:\n\n1. **Multiply 641 by the ones place digit (9) of 549:**\n   \\[\n   641 \\times 9 = 5769\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(600 \\times 9 = 5400\\), \\(40 \\times 9 = 360\\), \\(1 \\times 9 = 9\\)\n   - Sum: \\(5400 + 360 + 9 = 5769\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 641 by the tens place digit (40) of 549:**\n   \\[\n   641 \\times 40 = 25640\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(641 \\times 4 = 2564\\), then add a zero: \\(2564 \\times 10 = 25640\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 641 by the hundreds place digit (500) of 549:**\n   \\[\n   641 \\times 500 = 320500\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(641 \\times 5 = 3205\\), then add two zeros: \\(3205 \\times 100 = 320500\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   5769 + 25640 + 320500\n   \\]\n   - First, add \\(5769\\) and \\(25640\\):\n     \\[\n     5769 + 25640 = 31409\n     \\]\n   - Then add the result to \\(320500\\):\n     \\[\n     31409 + 320500 = 351909\n     \\]\n\nThus, the final product of 641 and 549 is \\(\\boxed{351909}\\).",
