s \\boxed{346020}.\n</think>\n\nTo find the product of 365 and 948, we break down the multiplication step by step using the place values of 948 (900, 40, and 8):\n\n1. **Multiply 365 by the ones place digit (8):**\n   \\[\n   365 \\times 8 = 2920\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(300 \\times 8 = 2400\\), \\(60 \\times 8 = 480\\), \\(5 \\times 8 = 40\\)\n   - Sum: \\(2400 + 480 + 40 = 2920\\)\n\n2. **Multiply 365 by the tens place digit (40):**\n   \\[\n   365 \\times 40 = 365 \\times 4 \\times 10 = 1460 \\times 10 = 14600\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(300 \\times 4 = 1200\\), \\(60 \\times 4 = 240\\), \\(5 \\times 4 = 20\\)\n   - Sum: \\(1200 + 240 + 20 = 1460\\)\n   - Multiply by 10: \\(1460 \\times 10 = 14600\\)\n\n3. **Multiply 365 by the hundreds place digit (900):**\n   \\[\n   365 \\times 900 = 365 \\times 9 \\times 100 = 3285 \\times 100 = 328500\n   \\]\n   - Calculation: \\(300 \\times 9 = 2700\\), \\(60 \\times 9 = 540\\), \\(5 \\times 9 = 45\\)\n   - Sum: \\(2700 + 540 + 45 = 3285\\)\n   - Multiply by 100: \\(3285 \\times 100 = 328500\\)\n\n4. **Sum all the results:**\n   \\[\n   2920 + 14600 + 328500 = 346020\n   \\]\n   - Intermediate sum: \\(2920 + 14600 = 17520\\)\n   - Final sum: \\(17520 + 328500 = 346020\\)\n\nThus, the product of 365 and 948 is \\(\\boxed{346020}\\).",
