en realized that when multiplied by 10 (for the tens place), it becomes 55,170. So that step was correct in the end. The key was catching that mistake and correcting it. So the process is correct.\n\nTherefore, following the template, the reasoning would be broken down into three steps corresponding to each digit of 896 (6, 90, 800), multiplying each by 613, then summing the results. The final sum is 549,248.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 613 and 896 is \\boxed{549248}.\n\n\n# Question:\nWhat is the product of 613 and 896?\n\n# Reasoning:\nLet's think step by step. 896 has three digits, so that we can reason in three steps.\n\n1. Multiply 613 by the ones place digit 6 of 896:\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 6 = 3678\n   \\]\n2. Multiply 613 by the tens place digit 90 (which is 9 in the tens place) of 896:\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 90 = 55170\n   \\]\n3. Multiply 613 by the hundreds place digit 800 (which is 8 in the hundreds place) of 896:\n   \\[\n   613 \\times 800 = 490400\n   \\]\n\nNow, sum all the step results:\n\\[\n3678 + 55170 + 490400 = 549248\n\\]\n\nSo, the final computed product is 549248.\n\n# Answer:\nThe product of 613 and 896 is \\boxed{549248}.",
