tandard way to confirm:\n\nMultiplying 889  \n\u00d7 112  \n________\n\nFirst multiply 889 by 2 (units place): 1,778  \nThen multiply 889 by 10 (tens place): 8,890  \nThen multiply 889 by 100 (hundreds place): 88,900  \nNow add them together:\n\n1,778  \n+8,890  \n=10,668  \n\nThen 10,668 +88,900 = 99,568. \n\nYes, that's the same result. So I think that's correct. \n\nTherefore, the product of 112 and 889 is 99,568.\n\n**Final Answer**\nThe product of 112 and 889 is \\boxed{99568}.\n\n\nTo find the product of 112 and 889, we break down 889 into its place values and multiply each part by 112, then sum the results.\n\n1. Multiply 112 by the ones place digit (9):\n   \\[\n   112 \\times 9 = 1008\n   \\]\n\n2. Multiply 112 by the tens place digit (80):\n   \\[\n   112 \\times 80 = 8960\n   \\]\n\n3. Multiply 112 by the hundreds place digit (800):\n   \\[\n   112 \\times 800 = 89600\n   \\]\n\nNext, we sum the results of these multiplications:\n\\[\n1008 + 8960 + 89600\n\\]\n\nFirst, add 1008 and 8960:\n\\[\n1008 + 8960 = 9968\n\\]\n\nThen, add the result to 89600:\n\\[\n9968 + 89600 = 99568\n\\]\n\nThus, the final computed product is \\(\\boxed{99568}\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{99568}\n\\]",
